blem-solving to convert prospects into customers. Variety, ambiguity, innovation, and ownership of complex problems are all big components of this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Account Executives in identifying a prospect’s fraud and compliance needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and deliver customized demos that showcase the impact of Sardine’s platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interface with Security teams to articulate our security posture and successfully complete security reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete RFPs for competitive opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create comprehensive Solution Designs that address our prospect’s needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with peers to improve all processes within the Sales Engineering team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work together with our product and engineering teams to identify areas for improvement in our product suite and help prioritize and design solutions.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll need:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years prior experience as a Sales Engineer, System Engineer, Solutions Engineer, or similar roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience in similar roles within the Risk, Fraud, or Compliance domain</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with APIs, a strong understanding of JSON, and proficiency in one or more of the following languages: Python, JavaScript, Ruby, Go, or Java. Bonus points for knowledge of web development principles and/or the ability to build internal tools using one of these languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills: you can dig into the 