er development, and meaningful opportunities to grow their ownership and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster a high-trust environment where engineers feel empowered to make decisions, learn through experimentation, and take accountability for outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead hiring, onboarding, and team development to build a strong, collaborative engineering team as n8n scales.</p></li></ul><h3>Drive execution and cross-functional alignment</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product, Design, and other stakeholders to align priorities, navigate trade-offs, and deliver meaningful product and platform outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create clarity and focus as priorities evolve, helping your team navigate uncertainty and embrace opportunities emerging from AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish lightweight processes and clear expectations that enable fast execution without compromising engineering quality, maintainability, or team health.</p></li></ul><h3>Lead with technical credibility and sound judgment</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide architectural and technical decisions, helping engineers navigate trade-offs around scalability, reliability, performance, and speed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a high bar for engineering excellence by mentoring engineers, challenging technical decisions constructively, and encouraging strong engineering practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dive into technical details or code when needed to unblock the team, while keeping your primary focus on people leadership and team effectiveness.</p></li></ul><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><h3><strong>Must-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌱 Engineering management experience:</strong> You have at least 1 year of experience as a first-line Engineering Manager, direct