ibility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The people who thrive at Rillet do not wait for assignments. They internalize the mission, design a strategy, and bring back results that are better, faster, and more creative than a manager could have asked for.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work revolves around our customers. The people who succeed here are energized by delivering what matters most, even when it was not part of the original plan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet is built on deep accounting expertise, and it takes people from many disciplines to build a category-defining company. You do not need to be an accountant to thrive here. You do need to care deeply about the problems we solve and the impact our customers can create. Together, we combine the precision of accounting with the speed, creativity, and ambition of AI-native software to power the financial core of the world’s fastest-growing companies while redefining what finance teams should expect from their software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who We Need</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building industry-defining accounting and finance software. We are looking for an experienced Deployment Lead to guide complex customer implementations and help finance teams successfully transition onto Rillet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is ideal for someone who has led ERP implementations and understands how to turn complex accounting and operational requirements into practical systems solutions. You may come from an ERP implementation firm, Big 4 finance transformation practice, systems consulting team, or a SaaS company serving finance organizations. You are comfortable owning multiple workstreams, advising senior stakeholders, and navigating the details of configuration, data migration, integrations, testing, and go-live.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will combine strong implementation judgment with a customer-first mindset—bringing structure to ambiguity, identifying risks early, and keeping customers and internal teams moving toward a successful launch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re primarily looking for teammates who are based near our New York City or San Francisco offices, or open to relocating.<strong> For this role, we’re also open to remote candidates based anywhere in the United States.</strong> Our hybrid schedule brings office-based team members together in person on Tuesdays and Thursdays, plus one additional flexible day each week. Some roles may spend more time in the office depending on the needs of the team.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead key parts of customer onboarding and deployment, helping ensure a smooth and timely implementation experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with internal teams across Product, Engineering, and Customer Success to execute implementation plans and solve customer problems quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn and analyze client accounting and finance workflows, then translate those needs into clear requirements and practical solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide customers through onboarding, training, change management, and adoption</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support data migration, reconciliations, systems setup, and integration coordination</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track milestones, drive follow-through, and keep internal and external stakeholders aligned throughout the onboarding process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify risks early, escalate issues quickly, and help keep customer launches on track</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build trust with customers by being responsive, thoughtful, and solutions-oriented</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain clear documentation and provide regular status updates to customers and internal sta