er acquisition process. Yet more to come.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Under the umbrella of the media company Bertelsmann, we have access to a global network of experts and strong financial support. By developing a state-of-the-art tech stack and highly skilled workforce, we aim to reach more mobile users than any other company in the world. If you want to grow your career in tech, challenge yourself in a high-performance environment, while having fun with great colleagues from all over the world, you’ve come to the right place!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find the whole world in one office. Boost your career with awesome people!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide L1, L2, and L3 technical support across macOS (80%), Windows, and Linux for accounts, devices, SaaS access, network, and meeting rooms, including leadership support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up, remove, and maintain technical equipment (meeting rooms, network) across our HQ offices (3) and maintain a park of 500+ workstations onsite in Hamburg and remotely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute account provisioning, device preparation, Day-1 desk support, and access revocation checklists during onboarding and offboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the IT warehouse, local inventory, loaner pools, and repair coordination with external logistics partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enforce proper security standards across all local machines and network environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain Confluence solutions and user guides while flagging repeat issues for self-service or automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the company's IT journey towards zero touch.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Who you are:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4-6 years of experience in IT Support roles or equivalent experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of working with Windows and Mac</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong troubleshooting and critical thinking skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independent, reliable way of working, high motivation, and hands-on mentality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expertise in various fields such as operating system administration, network security setup, infrastructure fallbacks, and process automation is highly valued. (While it's beneficial to have prior experience in these areas, we also welcome individuals who are eager to learn and passionate about these topics.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate fluently in both German and English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good to have: Experience in onboarding, coaching, and mentoring working students, interns, and other more junior colleagues</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">On-site Commitment: This role is 100% on-site at our Hamburg headquarters to ensure effective communication and hands-on management. But no worries, our office is amazing! 🙂</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Fuel for the Journey: Benefits to Support Your Ambitions</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Invest in Your Future: Regular feedback and our development program support your growth, helping you expand your skill set and achieve your career goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Easy Arrival to applike: From signing to settling in Hamburg, we’ve got you covered.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Live Your Best Life, at Work and Beyond: Flexible working hours. Enjoy 30 vacation days, and free access to an in-house gym with lots of different fitness classes and mental health support through our Employee Assistance Program (EAP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrive Where You Work: Enjoy the Alster Lake view from our central office with top-notch equipment, fun open spaces, and a large variety of snacks and drinks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join the Community! Participate in regular team and company events, including hackathons and social gatherings. We work together, and we celebrate together, too.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>The Interview Process:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1st: Interview with TA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case Study</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2nd: IT Support Team Lead and Senior IT Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3rd: Getting to know the IT Team and our Managing Director </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to create an inspiring work environment for amazing people to achieve extraordinary things. <strong>Be part of it</strong>!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skip writing cover letters. Tell us about your most passionate personal project, your desired salary, and your earliest possible start date. We are looking forward to your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome applications from people who will contribute to the diversity of our company.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/applike-group/it-support-technician-hamburg-36477","tags":["applike group"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1792582816},{"slug":"senior-people-business-partner-emea-munchen-196461","company_name":"Applied","title":"Senior People Business Partner - EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Applied Intuition, Inc. is powering the future of physical AI. Founded in 2017 and now valued at $15 billion, the Silicon Valley company is creating the digital infrastructure needed to bring intelligence to every moving machine on the planet. Applied Intuition services the automotive, defense, trucking, construction, mining and agriculture industries in three core areas: tools and infrastructure, operating systems, and autonomy. Eighteen of the top 20 global automakers, as well as the United States military and its allies, trust the company’s solutions to deliver physical intelligence. Applied Intuition is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California, with offices in Washington, D.C.; San Diego; Ft. Walton Beach, Florida; Ann Arbor, Michigan; London; Stuttgart; Munich; Stockholm; Bangalore; Seoul; and Tokyo. Learn more at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://applied.co">applied.co</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We are an in-office company, and our expectation is that full-time employees primarily work from their Applied Intuition office 5 days a week. However, we also recognize the importance of flexibility and trust our employees to manage their schedules responsibly. This may include occasional remote work, starting the day with morning meetings from home before heading to the office, or leaving earlier when needed to accommodate family commitments. This in-office expectation does not apply to contractor positions</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong><br />We're looking for a Senior People Business Partner in EMEA, supporting employees across Germany, Sweden, England, and other emerging geographies. You'll partner directly with country leaders at a company where the region is growing quickly, decisions are made in days, and priorities shift. You'll lead through influence, building trust with leaders in the region and with the People team at HQ in Sunnyvale, California.<br /><br />You are the senior People leader for the region, and the People function for EMEA runs through you. You'll own end-to-end People programs in every area starting at onboarding, and you'll be ready to direct stakeholders across the entire employee lifecycle, from onboarding through exit: regional leaders, managers, HQ People Operations, Payroll, Legal, Total Rewards, and local advisors and vendors. You set the priorities, assign the owners, and drive each issue to resolution.<br /><br />We expect our PBPs to lead with high agency, and this role carries that expectation further than any other. You'll set the regional People agenda, make the calls, and drive outcomes the way a regional Chief People Officer would, with specialist partners at HQ to pull in when you need them.<br /><br /><strong>Location:</strong> Munich, Germany<br /><strong>Reports to:</strong> Chief People Officer<br /><br /><strong>At Applied Intuition, you will:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the senior People leader and business strategist for EMEA.</strong> Understand where the regional business is going and bring leaders a clear point of view, with the tradeoffs of each option laid out. Translate business goals into talent decisions: org design, workforce planning, leveling, and succession. Use data to spot attrition risk, capability gaps, and structural problems before the business feels them, and treat your leaders as customers whose success is your measure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead end-to-end People programs for the region.</strong> Own the employee experience across the region: onboarding, payroll and benefits coordination, leave, compensation, performance, engagement, and employee relations, working within local employment requirements. Be scrappy when the moment calls for it: where infrastructure doesn't exist yet, build a working version yourself and refine it as you go.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct stakeholders across the employee lifecycle.</strong> Take the lead with HQ People Operations, Payroll, Legal, Total Rewards, and local advisors and vendors. Set priorities by risk, impact, and reversibility, assign owners and deadlines, and stay on each issue until the employee or manager has a complete answer. Build self-service resources, manager guides, and clear escalation paths so the regional People function doesn't depend on any one person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Connect Sunnyvale and EMEA.</strong> Make sure regional perspectives are part of global decisions early, and make global programs work locally. Know what has to stay consistent worldwide and what should flex by country, and bring HQ recommendations with the tradeoffs laid out, not just concerns. Treat each country in the region as its own environment, not as one market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead the region through growth and change.</strong> Support expansion into new countries and entities, reorganizations, and leadership transitions with a clear plan, narrative, and follow-through with managers and teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Increase talent density.</strong> Lead calibration, promotion, and talent review for the region. Identify and develop top talent, coach managers to raise the bar on their teams, and handle performance and employee relations issues with judgment, discretion, and dignity. Move fast and move safe.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are looking for someone who has:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of HR experience, with at least 3 years partnering directly with senior leaders, preferably in a high-tech environment, and experience as the sole or lead People leader for a region or country.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Breadth across the full HR function: employee relations, compensation, payroll and leave administration, performance management, org design, and engagement. You move comfortably from an individual employee's pay issue to a reorganization conversation with an executive on the same day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of employment practices and requirements in Germany, Sweden, and England and the judgment to know when a question needs local counsel or another specialist before you act.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong business acumen. You understand how the business makes money, where the constraints are, and how talent decisions affect outcomes, and you can speak that language with executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership and high agency. You've been the senior People leader for a region or business with minimal direction, directed partners across payroll, legal, benefits, and vendors without formal authority, and made decisions with incomplete information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong judgment. You know when to move fast, when to slow down an irreversible decision, and when to bring in partners, and leaders trust your read on sensitive, ambiguous situations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of influencing in both directions. You've advocated for a region with headquarters and challenged regional leaders when needed, and you can tell the difference between a legal requirement, a business need, and a preference.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of leading change, not just supporting it, including implementing global programs locally and guiding teams through growth or reorganization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency with data and clear, concise, direct communication, and the discipline to prioritize ruthlessly when everything feels urgent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business-level fluency in the local language is a plus. Comfort working across time zones with a People team based in California.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting engineering, research, or other highly technical organizations.</p>