><p style=";"></p><p>You will build on a strong foundation: an established sales team and a base of strong reference customers. Your mandate is to take this to the next level by building a predictable, scalable sales engine with full visibility across pipeline, accounts and forecast.</p><p style=";"></p><p>Around 75% of your time goes into hands-on sales leadership, and around 25% into business development and growth strategy. You will be a member of the commercial leadership team, alongside the regional VPs and the VP Marketing.</p><p><br /></p><p><strong>Job Duties<br /></strong></p><p style=";"></p><p><em>Pipeline and forecast</em></p><ul><li><p>Lead the weekly pipeline review across every rep, deal and stage.</p></li><li><p>Drive qualification rigour from first contact to close, ensuring forecasts are built on well-qualified opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Deliver a reliable monthly and quarterly forecast with clear insight into drivers and variance.</p></li><li><p>Be a hands-on CRM user and champion high standards of data quality and accuracy across the team.</p></li><li><p>Identify deals that need momentum early, create urgency and engage personally where it adds the most value.</p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p><em>Team leadership</em></p><ul><li><p>Set clear, measurable expectations for every seller, supported by structured 1:1s, deal reviews and coaching.</p></li><li><p>Develop team performance through coaching, enablement and effective talent management.</p></li><li><p>Lead the team through growth and change with a style that inspires people to follow.</p></li><li><p>Maintain transparent, proactive communication with senior leadership, raising topics early and always with a recommended next step.<br /></p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p><em>Customers and key accounts</em></p><ul><li><p>Personally own key accounts and strategic deals as a player-coach.</p></li><li><p>Build senior relationships across Kommunen, Länder and Bund, Stadtwerke and utilities, and infrastructure and telecom accounts.</p></li><li><p>Lead or steer public tenders (RFQ / RFP, Vergaberecht, framework agreements) together with pre-sales.<br /></p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p><em>Growth strategy and business development</em></p><ul><li><p>Build and own the growth plan for Germany, DACH and Poland: where the next 12–24 months of revenue will come from, by vertical, segment and channel.</p></li><li><p>Translate the plan into quarterly targets, headcount needs and channel priorities, and keep it current as a live commitment.</p></li><li><p>Align public-sector buying cycles with the company's annual planning cadence.</p></li><li><p>Identify white space in the existing customer base and the wider market.</p></li><li><p>Bring structured market intelligence to the commercial leadership team, always with a recommendation.</p></li><li><p>Orchestrate pre-sales, marketing and product through influence and collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style=";"></p><br /><br /><p><strong>Job Requirements:</strong></p><p style=";"></p><ul><li><p>10+ years in B2B sales, including 4+ years leading sales teams against revenue targets; around 15 years of overall experience is a useful guide.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>A hands-on operating style: you personally run the forecast, the weekly cadence, the pipeline and key accounts.</p></li><li><p>Public-sector exposure: familiarity with tender mechanics, procurement rules and public-sector buying timelines.</p></li><li><p>Experience in data or technology solution sales, ideally geospatial or adjacent technology, or data-driven solutions with a long, considered buying cycle.</p></li><li><p>Experience in a larger, structured corporate environment, combined with the motivation to apply that discipline in a company where your impact is direct and visible.</p></li><li><p>Leadership people follow: you set high standards, coach people to meet them and make sound people decisions.</p></li><li><p>Fluent German and fluent English.<br /></p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p><em>Nice to have</em></p><ul><li><p>Experience selling across several verticals such as government, utilities / Stadtwerke, telecom and infrastructure.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with Vermessung / Kataster and municipal planning buyers.</p></li><li><p>A regional growth plan you built and executed with measurable accountability.</p></li><li><p>Experience running several sales motions at once: direct enterprise, public sector, channel / partner and inbound.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on knowledge of public procurement, including RFPs, tenders and multi-year framework agreements.</p></li><li><p>Experience aligning public-sector sales cycles with the planning cadence of an investor-backed growth business.</p></li><li><p>Polish language skills.</p></li><li><p>Based in the Wetzlar / Frankfurt region<br /></p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p><strong>Benefits<br /></strong></p><ul><li><p>Real ownership: a clear growth mandate, genuine freedom to shape the plan, and a seat on the commercial leadership team.</p></li><li><p>A strong starting point: an experienced team and solid reference customers.</p></li><li><p>Competitive package: attractive base salary plus performance-related variable pay.</p></li><li><p>Company car.</p></li><li><p>28 days of annual leave, plus public holidays.</p></li><li><p>Supplementary health insurance: treatment by senior physicians and a private room, fully paid by Cyclomedia.</p></li><li><p>Company pension (Direktversicherung) with an employer contribution.</p></li><li><p>Learning and development: team coaching, online courses and individual training.</p></li><li><p>Team events: hiking, karaoke, treasure hunts and wine tastings are all part of how we get together.</p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p>Ready to lead the growth of one of our most important markets? Apply now and help us bring Cyclomedia's geospatial insights to the organisations shaping Central Europe.</p><p style=";"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cyclomedia-technology/head-senior-director-of-sales-central-europe-wetzlar-76021","tags":["Sales","bachelor's degree"],"job_types":["Full-time permanent","executive"],"location":"Wetzlar","created_at":1792581613},{"slug":"remote-principal-consultant-dach-germany-377093","company_name":"Avomind","title":"Principal Consultant - DACH","description":"<h3><strong>Job Description: </strong></h3><p>Our Client, a Data &amp; AI strategy and implementation firm is looking for a Senior/Principal Consultant to join their team. This role is key in the technical delivery of high-quality data management solutions for our customers. The Senior Consultant will work directly with clients, leading them through discovery, supporting design and implementation of scalable solutions. This position represents a combination of technical expertise, and ability to interact with customers, ensuring that solutions meet business requirements and deliver strategic value. Expertise in Master Data Management, Data Quality and Data Governance best practices from architectural and functional perspective is of key importance for this role, as well as hands-on experience in configuration of data management products, educating and providing guidance to clients.</p><p></p><h3>What You Will Do:</h3><p>Advisory</p><ul><li>Communicate with business and technical stakeholders to gather requirements, business needs, and strategic objectives</li><li>Educate stakeholders on technical and functional capabilities of the implemented software platforms, share best practices and drive decision making process</li><li>Prepare and conduct discovery workshops on specific topics to business and technical stakeholders</li><li>Map business requirements to technical capabilities, help to adjust customer expectations and support them with recommendations</li><li>Translate technical information appropriately to different levels of the client organization.</li></ul><p>Solution Design and Documentation</p><ul><li>Document requirements, user stories and test plans</li><li>Develop and document design for solution features including data models, quality, data access rules, workflows and user interfaces and data integration mappings</li></ul><p>Development and configuration leadership</p><ul><li>Configure the most critical components of the solution</li><li>Validate development done by other team members, develop testing and deployment plans</li><li>Provide oversight during development/configuration activities, testing and production deployment to the rest of the project team, developers and consultants. </li></ul><p>Pre-Sales Support</p><ul><li>Prepare customer presentations, proofs of concept, visual materials, and other tools for client presentations for business development purposes</li><li>Contribute to proposal and statement of work documentation by defining and defending needed scope of work, project approach and effort.<br></li></ul><h3>Who You Are:</h3><ul><li>Advanced German and English speaker</li><li>Highly focused on detail and results, with the ability to work with minimal supervision.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to build relationships with multinational technical team members</li><li>Advice and guide customer, demonstrate technical expertise and functional knowledge</li><li>Proactive identifier and communicator of technical risks</li><li>Demonstrated interest and ability to identify and assist in the sale of new project opportunities</li><li>Confident to tackle new business or technical challenges.</li><li>Disciplined curiosity: interest in asking "why" and synthesizing important findings into alternatives and recommendations</li><li>Excellent oral and written communicator</li><li>Able to travel to customer locations as needed</li></ul><p></p><h3>What You Bring:</h3><ul><li>More than 4 years of experience in the implementation of data management solutions or data management modules of enterprise grade ERP/CRM systems. Preferably - Master Data Management solution implementation using one of the following technologies: Informatica MDM, Stibo Step, Reltio, SAP MDG, TIBCO / Orchestra</li><li>Experience as a Configuration Specialist and Functonal Consultant</li><li>Experience driving discovery and design workshop, advisory meetings</li><li>Experience in SQL development, Java Script and REST API development</li><li>Experience in data modeling in both customer and product/material data domains</li><li>Experience in data platforms and analytics (Databricks, Snowflake, etc.)</li><li>Knowledge of data governance principles and frameworks</li><li>Experience in integration/migration SAP ERP (ECC and S/4 Hana)</li><li>Deep understanding of use cases for one or many industries</li></ul><p></p><h3>What We Offer:</h3><ul><li>Fast Track to Solution Architect / Managing consultant in growing regional organization</li><li>Customers are Fortune 500 corporate environments, and project work can occur in groups at customer sites or remotely in small teams.</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/avomind/remote-principal-consultant-dach-germany-377093","tags":["External - Commercial","Remote"],"job_types":[],"location":"Germany","created_at":1792581604},{"slug":"partner-channel-sales-manager-saas-fur-borsennotierte-ags-rhein-main-bawu-hybrid-frankfurt-am-main-155234","company_name":"Ilias Vassiliou & Team / headhunter.digital / Recruiting für Digital, Sales, IT, KI, Automation","title":"Partner & Channel Sales Manager • SaaS für börsennotierte AGs • Rhein-Main / BaWü (hybrid)*","description":"<p>Du bringst die richtigen Unternehmen zusammen und entwickelst daraus erfolgreiches SaaS-Geschäft?</p><p>Hier kannst du ein Partnernetzwerk aufbauen, das neue Kunden gewinnt und messbar zum Wachstum beiträgt. Du gestaltest die Channel-Sales-Strategie, gewinnst passende Partner und sorgst dafür, dass die Zusammenarbeit im Alltag funktioniert.</p><p>Du kannst zusätzlich Beziehungen zu börsennotierten AGs aufbauen, denn alle Unternehmen ab SDAX aufwärts gehören zur Kernzielgruppe (und teils schon bestehenden Nutzerbasis) unseres Mandanten.</p><p>Du bist also <strong>Channel Sales Manager</strong> und Marktgestalter:in in einem und trägst entscheidend dazu bei, die Nutzung <strong>einer führenden Corporate Reporting SaaS-Plattform im DACH-Markt</strong> und perspektivisch im europäischen Raum weiter auszubauen.</p><p>Diese <strong>kollaborative</strong> Content- & Design-Plattform wird u.a. genutzt für die Erstellung von Finanzberichten für Investoren und Analysten, z.B. von börsennotierten AGs, oder ESG Reports berichtspflichtiger Unternehmen (u.v.m.).</p><p>Du arbeitest eng mit dem Team in Frankfurt/Main sowie mit Kolleg:innen in der Schweiz aus Marketing, Sales, Produktmanagement und Consulting zusammen. Gleichzeitig bist du nah an den bestehenden Partnern dran und mit diesen im engen Austausch.</p><p><strong>Für wen ist dieser Job?</strong></p><p>Dieser Job ist ideal für dich, wenn du mind. 3 Jahre Berufserfahrung im Bereich B2B Software-Sales / SaaS und speziell Channel Sales hast. Relevant ist in dem Kontext, dass du den potentiellen Partnern <strong>Software-Lösungen sicher & routiniert demonstrieren</strong> kannst.</p><h2>Aufgaben</h2><p><strong>Du baust das Partnergeschäft aus – von der ersten Ansprache bis zum gemeinsamen Vertriebserfolg.</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Neue Partner gewinnen:</strong> Du identifizierst geeignete Beratungen, Agenturen, Implementierungs- und Technologiepartner, sprichst Entscheider aktiv an und überzeugst sie vom Nutzen einer Zusammenarbeit.</p></li><li><p><strong>Zusammenarbeit wirtschaftlich gestalten:</strong> Du entwickelst Modelle für Empfehlungen und Wiederverkauf, definierst finanzielle Anreize und verhandelst tragfähige Vereinbarungen.</p></li><l