ner noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a><strong> and the CEO Office</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> is building the future of payments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our global, multi-product payments network helps businesses move money, improve acceptance, manage fraud and turn payments into a competitive advantage. Headquartered in London, with offices around the world, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> is trusted by leading brands including eBay, DocuSign, Vinted, Uber, Klarna, Wise, Pinterest, Grab and Sony.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a career-defining opportunity at a generation-defining company. There is no finish line at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>: we set ambitious goals, build with intent and move at speed, always guided by our values as we work to create a brighter future for payments across the online ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are scaling a high-impact Strategy &amp; Operations team within the CEO Office to strengthen product delivery and execution across the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Manager, Strategy &amp; Operations, you will be a hands-on operator embedded in a designated Product team or pillar. Working alongside Product, Engineering and other functions, you will lead complex strategic and operational initiatives, align stakeholders, manage dependencies, resolve blockers and drive delivery from planning through launch. This is a business execution and operating leadership role—not primarily a consulting or process-improvement role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will use data and first-principles thinking to identify root causes, design practical solutions and build scalable operating mechanisms. The role offers high visibility with the CEO and executive team, with opportunities to grow into broader responsibilities across Product, Technology and the wider organisation.<br /></p><h2>How you’ll make an impact</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive strategic initiatives:</strong> Lead major cross-functional projects, create alignment, clarify ownership, manage risks and make sure initiatives launch effectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build scalable operating mechanisms:</strong> Develop practical standards and processes for planning, testing, launch readiness, governance, reporting and cross-functional decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve measurable business outcomes:</strong> Take ownership of specific processes or metrics where there is a clear opportunity to improve speed, quality or scalability.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Success means owning and delivering meaningful business projects—not simply diagnosing problems or redesigning processes in isolation. You will build trust with your Product team or pillar, take ownership of strategic initiatives and turn ambiguous priorities into clear, measurable plans that drive delivery through launch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we’re looking for: Background and core competencies</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You may come from strategy consulting, investment banking, product, technology, operations, professional services or a high-growth company. We’re looking for multiple years of experience in influential, ideally cross-functional roles in fast-paced, high-performance environments, with evidence of problem-solving, ownership and impact rather than a particular career path. Formative experience in STEM studies, high-level Manufacturing, or Professional Services (e.g., Management Consulting, Investment Banking) is valued but not essential</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Structured problem-solving:</strong> Exceptional ability to navigate ambiguity using first-principles thinking, data and sound judgement—not pattern-matching alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional delivery:</strong> Experience leading high-priority projects end to end, from framing the problem and aligning stakeholders to implementing solutions and delivering measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven decision-making:</strong> Ability to identify the right metrics, own data collection and analysis, and use dashboards or other tools to make progress, bottlenecks and performance visible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building and automation:</strong> Willingness to understand processes at ground level, then create or materially improve systems, workflows and operating capabilities from 0 to 1.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and impact:</strong> Take responsibility for complex work, follow through on the details and create lasting value for the teams and business you support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Influence and communication:</strong> Align and constructively challenge stakeholders without formal authority, communicate concisely and clearly at the right altitude and be willing to address difficult issues directly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/manager-operations-and-strategy-ceo-office-london-244801","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792593616},{"slug":"specialist-workplace-experience-london-152511","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Specialist, Workplace Experience","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to enable businesses and their communities to thrive in the digital economy. We’re the strategic payments partner for some of the best known fast-moving brands globally such as Wise, Hut Group, Sony Electronics, Homebase, Henkel, Klarna and many others. Purpose-built with performance and scalability in mind, our flexible cloud-based payments platform helps global enterprises launch new products and create experiences customers love. And it's not just what we build that makes us different. It's how.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We empower passionate problem-solvers to collaborate, innovate and do their best work. That’s why we’re on the Forbes Cloud 100 list and a Great Place to Work accredited company. And we’re just getting started. We’re building diverse and inclusive teams around the world — because that’s how we create even better experiences for our merchants and our partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role overview | Context</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will play a key part in delivering, optimising, and continuously evolving the London office experience across our UK operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own critical operational areas, driving performance through data and ensuring the workplace operates with precision, accountability, and consistency. Acting as a link between strategy and execution, you will translate workplace priorities into scalable processes, measurable outcomes, and high quality day to day experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will take ownership across workplace operations, vendor management, reporting, and governance, with the autonomy to make decisions and lead on key initiatives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a high impact role suited to someone who thrives in fast paced environments, brings a strong analytical mindset, and is motivated by raising the bar for workplace experience and operational excellence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will take a customer first approach to every interaction, proactively understanding employee and visitor needs, resolving issues through to completion, and using insight and data to continuously improve the workplace experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Role overview | Remit and Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Amongst other duties, this role will be primarily responsible for the below.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Leadership &amp; Delivery</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own day to day workplace operations, ensuring the office runs smoothly, safely, and consistently while delivering a seamless employee and visitor experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a visible and trusted on site point of contact, ensuring workplace spaces, services, and touchpoints are well maintained, well stocked, and delivered to a high standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct regular workplace walkthroughs to identify, resolve, and escalate issues before they affect employees or visitors, maintaining consistently high standards across presentation, safety, functionality, and hospitality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive operational excellence through strong execution, accountability, and continuous improvement across all Workplace activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and support workplace initiatives, aligning delivery with Workplace strategy, business needs, and opportunities to enhance the day to day employee experience and operational efficiency.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the UK Workplace budget end to end, including tracking, forecasting, variance analysis, and cost optimisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead procurement, PO management, and invoicing processes with accuracy and efficiency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Finance and Accounts Payable to resolve issues and improve processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage vendor commercials, including pricing negotiations and contract renewals</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vendor &amp; Contract Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain strong working relationships with key vendors and site partners, including building management, cleaning and maintenance providers, acting as the primary point of contact for day-to-day operational matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively manage supplier communication, ensuring expectations are clear, issues are resolved promptly, and services are delivered consistently to agreed standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive day to day vendor performance by monitoring service levels, holding suppliers accountable, providing regular feedback, and escalating risks or recurring issues where appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support contract management by maintaining accurate supplier records, tracking key dates and renewals, and coordinating contract administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to improve supplier performance, service delivery, and operational efficiency through regular reviews, performance reporting, and ongoing collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data, Reporting &amp; Performance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Workplace reporting frameworks, dashboards, and KPI tracking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver monthly and quarterly reporting across budget, operations, and workplace experience metrics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Combine operational data, service usage, employee feedback, and qualitative insight to identify trends, prioritise improvements, and measure the impact of changes on the employee experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track service performance measures including employee satisfaction, response and resolution times, service usage, recurring issues, and supplier performance; communicate outcomes and actions clearly to stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure team accountability to reporting standards and performance metrics</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder &amp; Site Operations</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting engagement with building management (e.g. CBRE), ensuring issue tracking, resolution, and accountability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong cross-functional relationships across People, Finance, and wider business teams including senior leadership</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance &amp; Sustainability</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Workplace compliance and reporting obligations (e.g. SECR, ESOS, energy reporting)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure alignment with regulatory, environmental, and company standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive improvements in sustainability performance</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Workplace Experience &amp; Projects</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee experience led services (e.g. Food &amp; Beverage), ensuring quality, consistency, and cost control</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Workplace Coordinator(s) to deliver an exceptional day to day employee experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead Workplace projects end to end and implement scalable process improvements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively identify opportunities to enhance workplace experience and operational efficiency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a sense of community through thoughtful workplace activations, local events, welcome moments, and connection opportunities that respond to employee needs and reinforce Checkout’s culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather employee feedback through regular informal engagement, surveys, and service touchpoints, ensuring concerns are acknowledged, resolved, and closed out with clear communication.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a <strong>workplace, operations, or culture experience role</strong>, ideally within a fast paced environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A customer first, hospitality minded approach, with the ability to build trusted relationships and create positive, personalised employee and visitor experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to <strong>own and manage operational functions</strong>, not just support them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong financial acumen, with experience in <strong>budget management, forecasting, and cost control</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence coordinating suppliers across hard and soft facilities management, responding to building issues, and escalating technical or compliance matters appropriately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing <strong>vendors and contracts</strong>, with a strong understanding of SLAs and performance management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly <strong>data driven mindset</strong>, with the ability to translate insights into action</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional <strong>organisation and attention to detail</strong>, with the ability to manage multiple priorities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong <strong>stakeholder management and influencing skills</strong>, confident working across all levels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to <strong>operate autonomously</strong>, take ownership, and make decisions with confidence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, solutions focused approach with a drive for <strong>continuous improvement</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills, both written and verbal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly self-sufficient and proactive, with sound judgement, a strong sense of ownership, and the ability to identify priorities and deliver solutions with minimal direction.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/specialist-workplace-experience-london-152511","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792593616},{"slug":"senior-ecommerce-content-strategist-london-314548","company_name":"Luzern eCommerce Group","title":"Senior eCommerce Content Strategist","description":"<p><strong>About Us</strong><br>Since 2003, Luzern eCommerce has been helping leading global brands grow their online business. We partner with brands including Panasonic, Reebok, Stokke, KIKO, Next, Twining's, Canon, Bondi Sands and Philips, helping them accelerate growth and deliver exceptional customer experiences across major marketplaces including Amazon and Zalando, branded webstores and social platforms.  </p>
<p>Backed by significant investment, Luzern is an international, technology-led eCommerce business with anambitious growth strategy. Our AI-enabled Channel Optimizer platform, combined with our eCommerce expertise, helps brands manage and grow their presence across increasingly complex digital channels.<br>As we continue to grow and evolve, we are looking for talented people who enjoy working in a fast-paced, collaborative environment and want to play an active role in the next stage of Luzern's development.  </p>
<p>The Senior eCommerce Content Strategist owns content strategy and execution across Amazon and the wider commerce ecosystem for Luzern's enterprise brand clients. Amazon is the primary focus — listings, A+/Premium A+ Content, Brand Store and related content — but the role is deliberately platform-agnostic in outlook, extending strategy and content guidance to other marketplaces, retailer sites (e.g. Tesco, Zalando,Otto) and D2C.  </p>
<p>The role is audit-led: content strategy is built from a structured read of customer and platform signals — reviews, search terms, AI-generated summaries, and the queries customers put to AI assistants and platform agents — combined with a quality assessment of current content (using a framework such as IDQ or equivalent) against Best-in-Class competitors and audience requirements. Strategy, messaging and content requirements follow from that evidence base, rather than from assumption.  </p>
<p>A defining part of the role is thinking beyond traditional platform search: strategies must consider how content needs to be structured and prepared to be discovered and surfaced by generative AI assistants (e.g ChatGPT) and in-platform shopping agents (e.g. Amazon's Rufus), alongside conventional marketplace and retailer search algorithms.  </p>
<p>The role sits as the senior content specialist within a small delivery pod, working alongside an SEO Executive and Designers. It carries direct client-facing responsibility: estimating, briefing, managing feedback and contributing to proposals and is responsible for reviewing the pod's output before it reaches the client. It does not carry resourcing, project management or formal line management responsibility.</p>
<h2>Tasks</h2>
<p><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></p>
<p><strong>Content Audits & Quality Assessment</strong><br>● Signal analysis: analyse customer reviews, search terms, AI-generated summaries, and the queries customers and AI agents put to platforms (e.g. Rufus prompts), to understand what content needs to do and where current content falls short.<br>● Quality benchmarking — review current platform content and score it against a content quality framework (e.g. IDQ or equivalent), benchmarking against Best-in-Class competitors and audience requirements.<br>● Findings to action — translate audit findings into a clear, prioritised view of content requirements that feeds directly into strategy.  </p>
<p><strong>Content Strategy Development</strong><br>● Amazon content ownership- develop and own content strategy and execution for listings, A+/Premium A+ Content, Brand Store and related Amazon content, as the role's primary focus.<br>● Cross-platform extension — extend strategy and content recommendations to other marketplaces,retailer sites (e.g. Tesco, Zalando, Otto) and D2C storefronts, adapting to each platform's content rules, algorithm and customer behaviour.<br>● Strategic framework - from audit findings, develop comms objectives, key messages and a messaging hierarchy for each client or category.<br>● Content requirements - define the content requirements, imagery and copy needed to deliverthe strategy, and the frameworks/guidelines the team and client can act on.<br>● Wireframes & mock-ups - develop A+ and Brand Store wireframes and mock-ups in collaborationwith the Designer, turning strategy into an executable creative direction.  </p>
<p><strong>AI & Agentic Discoverability</strong><br>● AI-ready content — build content strategies that account for how product and brand content is read, ranked and surfaced by generative AI assistants (e.g. ChatGPT) and in-platform shopping agents (e.g Rufus), alongside traditional search.<br>● Point of view — keep Luzern's thinking on AI/agentic discoverability current, and translate emerging platform and LLM behaviour into practical, sellable content recommendations.<br>● Alignment with SEO — partner with the SEO Executive so keyword and search strategy and content structure are aligned across traditional and AI-mediated discovery.  </p>
<p><strong>Testing & Performance Monitoring</strong><br>● A/B testing — recommend and run A/B tests (e.g. on A+ Content, Brand Store, imagery and messaging) to determine the most effective executional approach, rather than relying on opinion or precedent.<br>● Monitoring set-up - set up monitoring using Compass (or equivalent) to measure content effectiveness and implementation.<br>● Reporting on impact — track and report on content performance against strategy objectives, feeding learnings back into future audits and strategy.  </p>
<p><strong>Creative Briefing & Review</strong><br>● Strategic foundation - develop the strategy and messaging that underpins paid social, display and<br>marketplace advertising content.<br>● Creative briefs - write and own briefs for Designers producing static and video ad assets, translating strategy into clear creative direction.<br>● Creative review - review creative output against the brief, brand guidelines and platform requirements before client delivery.  </p>
<p><strong>Client Management</strong><br>● Client-facing delivery - present content strategy, recommendations and audit findings directly to client stakeholders.<br>● Estimates & scoping - prepare estimates and scopes of work for content workstreams.<br>● Briefs — shape and write content and creative briefs in response to client requirements.<br>● Feedback management — manage client feedback through to resolution, balancing client expectations against strategy and platform best practice.<br>● Proposals — contribute to and help prepare proposals and pitch content for new and existing client business.  </p>
<p><strong>Quality & Output Review</strong><br>● Senior review — review the SEO Executive's and Designers' work before it is sent to the client, checking it against strategy, brand guidelines and platform requirements.<br>● Direction — give feedback and direction to keep output consistent and on-strategy.  </p>
<p><strong>AI-Enabled Working</strong><br>● AI as a working method — use AI tools proficiently for content and competitive audits, for generating recommendations, and for producing or accelerating creative and written content — not only as a subject of strategy.<br>● Continuous improvement — identify and recommend where AI tools can improve the speed or quality of content production and audit work across the team.</p>
<h2>Requirements</h2>
<p><strong>What You Bring to the Role</strong></p>
<p>● Proven experience in Amazon content strategy and execution (listings, A+/Premium A+ Content, Brand Store, Amazon Posts), ideally within an agency or managed services environment.</p>
<p>● Working knowledge of content requirements across at least one other marketplace or major retailer platform (e.g. Tesco, Zalando, Otto) and D2C.</p>
<p>● Experience running content audits — analysing reviews, search terms, AI-generated summaries and customer/AI-agent queries — and scoring content quality (e.g. IDQ or equivalent) against best-in-Class standards.</p>
<p>● Experience translating audit findings into content strategy: comms objectives, key messaging, messaging hierarchy, and content requirements for imagery and copy.</p>
<p>● Experience developing or briefing A+ and Brand Store wireframes and mock-ups, working closely with designers.</p>
<p>● Experience designing and running A/B tests to determine the most effective executional approach, and setting up performance monitoring (e.g. Amazon Compass or equivalent) to track results.</p>
<p>● Strong understanding of how AI assistants and platform shopping agents (e.g. ChatGPT, Rufus)surface and rank product content, and how content should be structured to support this.</p>
<p>● Confident, credible client-facing communicator — comfortable presenting strategy, leading feedback conversations, and owning estimates and proposals.</p>
<p>● Experience briefing creative teams for paid social/display advertising, across both static and video formats.</p>
<p>● Demonstrable, hands-on use of AI tools for research, auditing and content production, not just familiarity in principle.</p>
<p>● Strong copywriting and content editing skills, with a close eye for brand and platform compliance.</p>
<p>● Comfortable reviewing and giving constructive feedback on the work of SEO and design peers.</p>
<p><strong>Desirable</strong></p>
<p>● Experience across multiple international marketplaces or retail media platforms.</p>
<p>● Familiarity with SEO fundamentals, to collaborate effectively with the SEO Executive.</p>
<p>● Experience contributing to new business pitches or proposals.</p>
<p>● Category experience relevant to Luzern's enterprise brand client base.</p>
<h2>Benefits</h2>
<p><strong>What We Offer</strong><br>● Competitive salary and benefits<br>● Hybrid Working Model<br>● Great working environment with a passionate, collaborative team<br>● Continuous learning & career development<br>● The opportunity to work with some of the world's leading brands across the most exciting marketplaces</p>
