br><br>First off, it's best I introduce myself (person behind the keyboard here). It’s not the norm on a job advert, but I think it’s important you get introduced to who you might be working with for a long time early on.<br><br>I'm Luca, Chief Financial Officer at DFYNE, and I'm looking for someone who can help us continue building a world-class finance function as we scale globally.<br><br>This isn't a traditional management accountant role where you'll only focus on month-end reporting from a distance. We're looking for someone who takes ownership of accurate and timely management accounts while remaining hands-on across accounts payable, fixed asset management, lease accounting, financial controls, and commercial analysis.<br><br>You'll be responsible for ensuring financial information is reliable, insightful, and delivered on time, whilst maintaining strong processes that keep the day-to-day finance operation running smoothly. You'll partner with teams across the business, challenge costs where appropriate, identify risks and opportunities, and support the continued growth of DFYNE through sound financial management.<br><br><strong>Attitude:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Ownership mentality</li><li>Detail obsessed</li><li>Commercially curious</li><li>Problem solver</li><li>Calm under pressure</li><li>Continuous improvement mindset</li></ul><br><br><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong><br><br><strong>1. Management Accounts & Month-End Reporting:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Prepare monthly management accounts, including profit and loss, balance sheet, and supporting schedules, to agreed deadlines.</li><li>Post and review accruals, prepayments, depreciation, amortisation, and other month-end journals; maintain clear supporting working papers.</li><li>Complete and review balance sheet reconciliations, investigate differences, and resolve outstanding items.</li><li>Analyse actual results against budget, forecast, and prior periods, explaining material variances and cost trends to management.</li><li>Support budgeting, forecasting, cash-flow planning, and improvements to management reporting.</li><li>Ensure accurate cut-off, allocation of costs to departments and cost centres, and completeness of month-end liabilities.</li><li>Work with the Finance Team Lead on audit preparation, financial controls, and process improvements.</li></ul><br><br><strong>2. Fixed Assets & Right-of-Use (ROU) Asset Accounting:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Maintain and reconcile the Fixed Asset Register (FAR), ensuring accurate accounting for capital expenditure (CapEx), additions, disposals, and depreciation calculations.</li><li>Manage Right-of-Use (ROU) asset schedules and lease liabilities in accordance with relevant accounting standards (IFRS 16 / FRS 102), ensuring monthly lease interest and depreciation journals are accurately posted.</li><li>Review purchase invoices and CapEx requests to ensure correct capitalisation treatment versus operational expense (OpEx).</li><li>Perform periodic physical asset verifications/audits and reconcile asset register balances to general ledger control accounts.</li><li>Prepare lease schedules, impairment reviews, and disclosures for month-end and year-end statutory audit reporting.</li></ul><br><br><strong>3. Daily Finance Inbox & Invoice Control:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Manage and clear the finance inbox daily, with visible Processed/Actioned and pending categories to support seamless handovers.</li><li>Register 100% of incoming invoices in NetSuite within two working days and maintain visibility of future payment liabilities.</li><li>Verify supplier invoice details, dates, values, and UK VAT treatment; accurately code invoices to general ledger accounts and cost centres.</li><li>Assess expenditure for value for money; query unexpected charges with department heads and place unresolved invoices on hold.</li></ul><br><br><strong>4. Reconciliations & Financial Control:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Regularly review and cleanse the accounts payable ledger, resolving aged balances, unapplied payments, and debit notes.</li><li>Reconcile supplier statements, the AP sub-ledger, fixed asset registers, lease schedules, and the general ledger before month-end close.</li><li>Keep AP postings aligned with bank payment schedules and investigate discrepancies promptly.</li><li>Maintain accurate, audit-ready records and comply with applicable HMRC VAT and record-keeping requirements.</li></ul><br><br><strong>5. Specialist Logistics Accounting:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Process outbound shipping invoices weekly, clearing relevant inbox items before posting; post matching journals on the same day for accurate cost-centre reporting.</li><li>Register returns logistics invoices on receipt, complete checks using the available checker, and post required journals.</li></ul><br><br><strong>Experience Needed:</strong><br><br><ul><li>AAT-qualified, part-qualified ACCA/CIMA, or qualified by experience with substantial relevant responsibility.</li><li>Demonstrable hands-on experience preparing monthly management accounts and completing month-end close.</li><li>Practical experience in maintaining fixed asset registers, calculating depreciation, and managing capital expenditure accounting.</li><li>Strong practical accounts payable experience, including high-volume invoices, supplier reconciliations, and payment runs.</li><li>Experience with NetSuite or a comparable cloud ERP; sound Excel skills for reconciliations and reporting.</li></ul><br><br><strong>Skills:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Understanding of lease accounting principles and Right-of-Use (ROU) asset management under IFRS 16 or FRS 102.</li><li>Confident with journals, accruals, prepayments, balance sheet reconciliations, and variance analysis.</li><li>Good understanding of UK VAT, HMRC documentation requirements, general ledger coding, and financial controls.</li><li>Organised, accurate, and commercially aware; comfortable challenging costs and working independently to deadlines.</li><li>Able to communicate effectively with department heads, suppliers, and senior finance colleagues.</li></ul><br><br><strong>So, what’s in it for you?:</strong><br><br>If you’ve made it this far down without being put off, brilliant, I’d love to hear from you. Besides a work family and a great place to work, you’ll have an opportunity to grow with the company, be a part of the journey, and have a vital input into helping continue the crazy growth we’ve already seen.<br><br>You’ll be part of a high challenge, high reward culture.<br><br><strong>Salary:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Starting from £52,430 annually.</li></ul><br><br><strong>What will aid a successful application with DFYNE:</strong><br><br><ul><li>Cover letter</li><li>Completed questionnaire</li></ul><br><br><strong>Equality and diversity monitoring</strong><br><br>DFYNE wants to meet the aims and commitments set out in our equality policy. This includes not discriminating under the Equality Act 2010.<br><br>Please complete this form to help us understand the diversity of our candidates.<br><br>Completing this form is voluntary and the information provided will be kept confidential. The information is going to be used to help us understand the diversity of our organisation.<br><br>None of the information you provide will be linked to your application and is completely anonymous<br>(https://forms.gle/LQiAKzDb6CUzS9Bm7)<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/olr-holdings-ltd-trading-as-dfyne/senior-finance-officer-uddingston-393665","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["professional / experienced"],"location":"Uddingston","created_at":1792589490},{"slug":"global-solutions-architect-cloud-london-413125","company_name":"Rubrik","title":"Global Solutions Architect - Cloud","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Solutions Architect - Cloud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Rubrik Professional Services is hiring a Global Solutions Architect to serve as our most senior technical authority for public cloud. This is a global, individual-contributor role at Technical Director level. You will set the architectural direction for how Rubrik is designed, deployed, and operated in the world’s most demanding cloud environments, and you will carry that direction personally into our most strategic customer engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be deployed where technical risk is highest: flagship accounts, first-of-a-kind architectures, and the engagements whose outcome sets the pattern everyone else follows. Between those engagements, you will convert what you learned into the reference architectures, service offerings, and enablement that raise the capability of every architect and consultant in the field. Your impact is measured by the quality of the practice you leave behind, not the hours you personally bill.&lt;br&gt;We are looking for depth in public cloud architecture first. Deep Rubrik product expertise is expected to be built on the job. If you have architected large-scale data, storage, or security platforms across AWS, Azure, and GCP, and you can learn a new platform quickly and completely, we want to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the global cloud architecture standard for Rubrik Professional Services, reference architectures, design patterns, guardrails, and documented anti-patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the final technical escalation point for cloud architecture decisions on strategic engagements worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the technical shape of our cloud service offerings: what we sell, how it is scoped, and what good delivery looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish Rubrik PS’s position on emerging cloud capabilities and translate them into deployment guidance before customers ask&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the hardest engagements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own architecture and design on the most complex, highest-visibility customer engagements globally, multi-region, multi-cloud, and multi-regulator estates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as trusted advisor to customer CIO, CTO, Chief Architect, and CISO stakeholders, and defend design decisions in front of customer architecture review boards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Pre-Sales on strategic pursuits: technical validation, level of effort, and honest risk assessment on the deals we cannot afford to get wrong&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead briefings and multi-day design workshops on site and remotely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale yourself through the practice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the intellectual property that multiplies your reach, reference architectures, deployment automation, design templates, decision trees, and delivery accelerators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and technically develop Solutions Architects and senior consultants across all theatres; raise the ceiling of the practice, not just your own output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define technical competency standards and enablement for cloud within Professional Services, and help set the hiring bar through technical interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Rubrik Professional Services externally at conferences, customer advisory boards, and in published technical material&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence the product&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the field’s most credible voice into Product Management and Engineering, backed by evidence from our largest deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape roadmap priorities, supportability, and cloud-native feature direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Support and Customer Success on systemic technical issues before they become patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with PS Operations and leadership to turn field learning into better scoping models, estimates, and delivery methodology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15+ years overall experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including 8+ years as a handson cloud architect at enterprise scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated ownership of architecture&lt;/strong&gt; for multi-region, multi-account or multi-subscription cloud estates, in a large enterprise or a consulting / professional services organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expert-level AWS and Azure&lt;/strong&gt;; GCP strongly preferred. Genuine depth across compute, storage, networking, identity, and encryption / key management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep understanding of enterprise data protection and cyber resilience&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;RTO and RPO modelling, immutability, backup and recovery design, isolated and air-gapped recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working fluency in cloud security and compliance frameworks&lt;/strong&gt; and how they constrain design in regulated industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong automation background&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; infrastructure as code (Terraform, CloudFormation, Bicep), scripting (Python, PowerShell), API-first integration, and CI/CD (Strong Automation Background)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of influence without authority&lt;/strong&gt; across a global, matrixed organization and multiple time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive-grade communication&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; credible with a customer’s CIO and their principal engineer on the same day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence of building reusable technical IP&lt;/strong&gt;, not only delivering successful projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ability to learn a complex new platform to expert depth, quickly.&lt;/strong&gt; Prior Rubrik experience is not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Occasional travel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes and containerized workload architecture; cloud-native and managed database platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS data protection experience (Microsoft 365, Salesforce, and similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior Principal, Distinguished, or Technical Director title within a vendor professional services organization or a major systems integrator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional or expert-level certifications (AWS Solutions Architect – Professional, Azure Solutions Architect Expert, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An established public technical presence — talks, writing, open source, or community leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
