igence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powered by the sector’s largest proprietary operations dataset, Plentific’s AI agents act, orchestrating processes and transforming property operations in real-time, helping owners, operators, service providers and residents streamline operations, unlock efficiencies and enhance the resident experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Its solutions span repair diagnostics, work order management, resident self-service, contractor and field service management, inspections and compliance. Acting as an integration layer, Plentific enables a real-time ecosystem and helps providers build resilient supply chains that prevent backlogs and ensure timely delivery of works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><br /></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Events Marketing Manager at Plentific is responsible for developing and executing key marketing initiatives to drive client acquisition, networking and retention, and revenue growth. This role focuses on event planning, digital marketing execution and optimisation, and content creation, including website updates, email campaigns, and agency management. The Events Marketing Manager will lead internal and external events, webinars, partner marketing initiatives, and social media efforts while overseeing sales enablement and inbound marketing. Close collaboration with the commercial and product teams is essential to align marketing campaigns with business objectives and support revenue generation. The role reports to the Marketing Director and covers events across the UK and Germany.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute event marketing plans for physical and digital formats aligned with company objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own