<li>Own and manage the full bid lifecycle from opportunity qualification and bid planning through to submission, clarification, contract handover and post-bid review.</li>
<li>Develop and maintain clear bid plans covering deliverables, responsibilities, dependencies, review stages, approvals, resources and deadlines.</li>
<li>Lead bid kick-offs, progress reviews, solution workshops and final submission reviews, creating clarity and accountability across all contributors.</li>
<li>Coordinate and actively manage internal stakeholders, external consultants and specialist partners, challenging delays, unclear ownership or insufficient contributions.</li>
<li>Identify bid risks, dependencies, gaps and decision requirements early, escalating where necessary to protect quality, commercial viability and timelines.</li>
<li>Lead bid qualification and go/no-go assessments, ensuring that client requirements and commercial, technical, operational and delivery implications are fully understood.</li>
<li>Develop the bid strategy, win themes, key messages and overall proposal structure in collaboration with relevant stakeholders.</li>
<li>Ensure that submissions are compliant, persuasive, commercially competitive and operationally deliverable, constructively challenging assumptions and proposed commitments.</li>
<li>Own the overall quality and consistency of proposal content, turning cross-functional input into one clear, client-focused response.</li>
<li>Maintain an accurate tender pipeline and clear reporting on opportunity status, key dates, resource requirements, risks and decisions.</li>
<li>Improve bid-management tools, governance and reusable content, including Jira-based planning and appropriate use of AI-supported bidding solutions.</li>
<li>Ensure a structured handover of successful bids, including commitments, assumptions, risks, dependencies, SLAs and implementation obligations, to Delivery and Operations.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Your profile</h2>
<h2>What We're Looking For</h2>
<ul>
<li>Proven experience leading complex bids, proposals or tender processes from qualification through to submission and handover.</li>
<li>Strong project-management skills, including planning, stakeholder coordination, risk management, governance and action tracking.</li>
<li>Confidence coordinating and constructively challenging contributors across different functions and levels of seniority.</li>
<li>Ability to create accountability and maintain momentum without relying on formal authority.</li>
<li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to turn complex input into clear and persuasive proposals.</li>
<li>Strong commercial judgement and the ability to understand client priorities, operational constraints and business risks.</li>
<li>Ability to identify gaps, dependencies and unrealistic commitments early and drive timely decisions.</li>
<li>Highly organised and comfortable managing several concurrent deadlines and changing priorities.</li>
<li>Experience with public-sector procurement, framework agreements or infrastructure tenders would be highly advantageous.</li>
<li>Experience in EV charging, energy, transport, mobility, utilities or related infrastructure, and familiarity with Jira, CRM or proposal-management tools, would be beneficial.</li>
</ul>
