&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/affirm/senior-manager-technical-recruiting-18758","tags":["Talent Acquisition"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792562113},{"slug":"sales-director-emea-london-325029","company_name":"Talos Trading","title":"Sales Director, EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2018, Talos provides institutional-grade trading technology for the global digital asset market, powering many of the major players in the crypto ecosystem. Our mission is clear: to advance the mass adoption of digital assets by seamlessly connecting institutions to the digital asset ecosystem. We are committed to building the most innovative and trusted platform in the world, supporting the entire trading lifecycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Talos, you’ll find an environment that champions kindness and respect, values diverse perspectives, and upholds inclusivity at every turn. We believe every member of our team brings invaluable insights and abilities that drive Talos forward. In our pursuit of excellence, we foster a culture of trust, integrity, collaboration, and mutual growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a tight-knit yet globally distributed team of highly experienced engineers and business leaders, with hubs in New York, London, Singapore, and Cyprus. You’ll be part of a hybrid-friendly environment where your unique talents and insights will play a crucial role in building something extraordinary.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Sales Director, EMEA</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior sales opportunity for an experienced commercial leader to drive Talos’s growth with banks and TradFi institutions as institutional finance moves into digital assets and tokenized, multi-asset trading.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Sales Director at Talos, you will own new business and key relationships across the UK, with a focus on banks and TradFi institutions entering digital assets. You will run the full deal lifecycle, from origination and discovery through solutioning, trials and close, partnering closely with Solutions and Account Management to make sure clients are set up for long-term success.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talos runs a structured, consultative sales environment. This role suits someone with an established TradFi network, a proven record of originating revenue, and the ability to clearly articulate how institutional trading infrastructure is changing.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Originate and close new business across banks, broker-dealers and TradFi institutions, alongside Talos’s core client segments including hedge funds, market makers, prime brokers and digital asset service providers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use and expand your network of senior bank and TradFi relationships to build a high-quality pipeline from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead senior-level discovery and demo conversations, mapping institutional workflows and requirements to Talos’s product capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Position Talos clearly within the evolving digital asset ecosystem, translating TradFi requirements across connectivity, risk, compliance and workflow into Talos’s value proposition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage and grow an existing book of business in partnership with Account Management, driving retention, expansion and executive-level relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate cross-functionally with Solutions, Account Management, Product and Engineering to advance deals and make sure client commitments are accurate and deliverable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture and communicate client and market insights to inform product roadmap and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain disciplined pipeline management and forecasting in Salesforce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a senior Talos presence in the London market, representing Talos at industry conferences and client events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share expertise and informally mentor junior members of the sales team.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of client-facing sales or commercial experience within institutional financial services, fintech or enterprise SaaS serving capital markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An established network of active relationships across banks and TradFi institutions, particularly in the UK and Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of originating and closing new business, with quantifiable results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of TradFi market structure and institutional trading workflows. Experience in FX, fixed income, equities or multi-asset trading environments is highly valued.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with digital assets is advantageous but not required. You should bring genuine interest in how TradFi is adopting digital assets and tokenization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to lead consultative, senior-level sales conversations and explain complex infrastructure in clear, client-friendly terms.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong commercial judgment, with the discipline to set realistic client expectations and avoid overcommitting on product or timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-directed, high-ownership approach: you can build a pipeline and maintain momentum independently, without ramp-up or close guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, team-first mindset, comfortable in a fast-paced, distributed environment with a high degree of autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in London, or able to work from the London office.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Our Sales Approach</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talos operates a systematic, consultative sales process built around a simple principle:<em> listen first, sell second</em>. We take the time to understand a client's workflows, constraints, and goals before positioning a solution. We sell what we have - with deep product mastery and honest conversations about what's on the roadmap and what isn't.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We maintain a balanced pipeline across focus segments, use Salesforce rigorously to track progress, and hand off every closed deal with a documented account plan so the relationship starts on solid footing from day one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We play the long game. Underpromise, overdeliver, and build the kind of relationships that compound over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>More about Talos </strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out these videos and links to learn more about Talos and our culture!</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spotlight Article: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.drw.com/vc/updates/drw-vc-portfolio-company-spotlight-anton-katz-talos/"><u>Talos Snapshot by DRW</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Podcast: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-gDUxXkBMr8&amp;t=62s/"><u>2023 episode with co-founders Anton &amp; Ethan</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Website: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.talos.com/"><u>Explore Talos: Products, Investors, Team &amp; More</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case Studies: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.talos.com/insights?insight-category=Case+Studies"><u>Real world examples of client solutions</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awards: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.talos.com/insights/talos-wins-best-trading-platform-at-hedgeweek-global-digital-assets-awards-2024/"><u>Talos Wins Hedgeweek Global Digital Assets Award 2024</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.talos.com/insights/forbes-names-talos-one-of-americas-best-startup-employers-for-the-second-year-in-a-row/"><u>Award-winning, Forbes-listed, low-attrition team</u></a></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Andreessen Horowitz re: Talos: "The company best suited to drive institutional adoption is one that understands traditional capital markets deeply and is forward-thinking enough to fully grasp the promise of crypto. Talos is that company."</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also enjoy a comprehensive array of competitive benefits, regardless of your location, within our warm, welcoming, and ambitious company culture. Some of our benefits include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement plan contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited Vacation + a PTO bonus: Employees that take 15 days of vacation, with 5 days being consecutive, receive a $2000 USD bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus and stock ownership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave for 20 weeks, after 1 year of service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global offsites and team outings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-time stipend towards at-home office set-up for all employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A wellness credit of $50 accrued monthly, to go towards things like gym memberships, ski-passes, and work out classes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A lunch credit of $25 USD towards lunches for days in-office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Donation matching up to $100 USD annually</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Other in-office perks: Catered lunches on Tuesdays, snacks, and drinks</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talos is proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer.  We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, sexual stereotypes, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.  Talos is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for candidates with disabilities in our recruiting process.  If you need any assistance or accommodations due to a disability, please let us know at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- /><br />To protect the interests of all parties, Talos Trading, LLC and its affiliates (“Talos”)<strong> strongly discourage submission of unsolicited resumes from any source other than directly from a candidate</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talos will NOT pay fees, commissions or compensation of any kind (“Fees”) for any placement or hire resulting from the receipt of an unsolicited resume. Talos will consider any candidate for whom an Agency has submitted an unsolicited resume to have been referred by the Agency free of any charges or fees and Talos reserves the right to contact, interview, and hire the candidate directly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agencies, search firms, recruitment firms and similar organizations (“Agencies”) must obtain advance written approval from Talos’s internal recruiting team to submit resumes, AND must sign a valid fully executed placement agreement with Talos in order to be eligible to receive any Fees from Talos. Talos will not pay a Fee to any Agency that does not have such agreement in place.  By submitting a resume without a signed agreement, you acknowledge and accept these terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">© Talos Trading, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- /><br />By submitting your application and pursuing job candidacy, you consent to the processing of your personal information in connection with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://www.talos.com/legals/employee-privacy-policy">Applicant &amp; Employee Privacy Notice</a>. </p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/talos-trading/sales-director-emea-london-325029","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792561215},{"slug":"global-event-producer-london-103049","company_name":"Pmmalliance","title":"Global Event Producer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">When it comes to digital communities, The Alliance is leading the way. Product marketing, sales enablement, product-led growth, AI, customer success, CMOs, you name it, we’re home to thriving communities for them all.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 160,000+ professionals across our communities and a constant stream of events, memberships, and learning products, we help individuals and teams grow faster in their careers. We work with some of the world’s most recognisable companies and pride ourselves on being a high-impact learning partner, not just another events business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re ambitious, we move quickly, and we’re still early in the journey. That means real ownership, a steep learning curve, and plenty of opportunity to shape what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our pioneering<strong> conference production team</strong> deliver market-dominating events across the tech, marketing and finance industry. They bring together leading minds to share the latest trends, challenges and opportunities facing companies, the tactics and tools needed to drive results, and a forum to make meaningful connections.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join them and you’ll develop your research skills, flex your commercial acumen and nail project management.  If you’re craving hands-on business experience within a high-growth B2B start-up, there’s no better place. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oh, and did we mention the opportunity to travel internationally?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carry out research, and engage with our community to understand the challenges and opportunities facing professionals in that space.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn how to engage with, and secure, speakers from the world's best-known brands and most exciting start-ups. Think TikTok, Microsoft, Peloton, &amp; Uber.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curate the event content, format and agenda to create unmissable attendee experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the product owner, you’ll be the command centre for your event, responsible for its successful launch, delivery and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Project manage a team of marketing, sales and  community managers - working closely together to<strong> </strong>drive sponsored partnerships, ticket revenues, and attendance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop your leadership skills and test your initiative and adaptability as you motivate the team to reach and exceed ambitious targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain event websites, develop your copywriting skills &amp; contribute to content-led promotion, including video and social media.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the event on-site, or virtually, working alongside our operations team to deliver a world-class experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">it doesn’t stop there - after a short time, it's realistic that you’ll get involved in overseeing a team, producing events and programs in new markets, or helping us grow in new directions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This might be for you if…</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a natural relationship builder and a confident and articulate communicator </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have great research skills, can grasp complex topics and spot business trends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want the chance to take ownership of tasks and see them through </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Seeing the results of your hard work and how it affects business outcomes excites you</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re commercially minded and curious</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are willing and proactive in learning, and with a can-do attitude</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're ambitious, and entrepreneurial and enjoy working towards targets </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're highly organised - you’ll be juggling several ongoing projects week in, week out. Accuracy and professionalism are essential. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a team player - success doesn’t happen in a vacuum, we need everyone to be rallied around the same goals and help each other to achieve them </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly structured corporate schemes don’t appeal to you- a fun, fast-paced, supportive, and social team is more your speed. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Base Salary</strong> £280,00-30,000 depending on experience (OTE year 1 £40K, OTE increases year 2 onwards)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is Hybrid with 2 days/week in the London office.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">___________________</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Benefits</h2><h3>Time off &amp; flexibility</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>34 days’ paid holiday</strong> including UK Bank holidays and a day off on your birthday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible working hours</strong>: our core hours are 10am–4:30pm, with the flexibility to structure your working day between 8am and 8pm around when you work best</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work from where works for you</strong>: choose to work remotely within the UK or hybrid from our London office. Our office is always open to the wider team whenever you fancy coming in</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WFH Kit:</strong> a comprehensive tech setup, plus a dedicated WFH equipment budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A well-stocked office</strong>: snacks, drinks and fresh fruit available in our London office</p></li></ul><h3>Health &amp; wellbeing</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private Medical and Dental Insurance</strong> with Bupa</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life Insurance: </strong>cover worth 4x your annual salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On-demand therapy &amp; coaching</strong>: company sponsored access to therapy and career coaching through Spill</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wellness perks</strong>: discounts on gym memberships, fitness and wellness classes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cycle to Work &amp; Workplace Nursery schemes</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks at Work</strong>: access to a wide range of corporate discounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Monthly flexible benefits allowance</strong> through ThanksBen (£50/month in year one, £100/month in year two and £165/month from year three), giving you extra flexibility to spend on the benefits that matter most to you</p></li></ul><h3>Learning &amp; development</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A growing personal L&amp;D budget </strong>(starting at £500 per year and increasing with tenure to £3,000 per year)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dedicated L&amp;D or volunteering time</strong>: one paid day every quarter to invest in your development or support a cause you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited access to our internal Academy</strong>: including courses, learning resources and professional certifications</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">______________________________________</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Community and Inclusion<br /></strong><em><br />We are committed to creating a workplace that is free from discrimination and bias, and where everyone has equal opportunities to succeed and contribute. We acknowledge that our work here is never done - and we promise to continue striving for inclusivity every day.<br /><br />If you’re worried you don’t quite hit all the requirements we’ve listed, don’t let that hold you back from submitting your application! Unique backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives are essential for our ability to innovate and grow, so if you think you’d be a great fit then we’d love to hear from you.<br /></em><strong>We are The Alliance - in more ways than one.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: £28K – £30K • Offers Commission</p><ul><li> • £28K – £30K • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pmmalliance/global-event-producer-london-103049","tags":["*Event Production"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hybrid","created_at":1792561215},{"slug":"head-of-brand-and-creative-united-kingdom-403240","company_name":"Lyrebird Health","title":"Head of Brand and Creative","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Head of Brand and Creative</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The UK is Lyrebird's most important new market, and you'll own how we show up in it. You'll co-develop Lyrebird's brand strategy and lead its rollout across the UK, covering media, communications, campaigns, research, partnerships, agency and budget management, and the brand measurement that proves it's working. You'll also own the creative bar for everything Lyrebird makes globally. That means the taste and quality of the work, plus the operations, agencies and systems that let in-house and external teams produce world-class creative at pace. This is a senior leadership hire at a foundational moment: you'll shape how Lyrebird looks, sounds and feels as it scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role suits someone who moves easily between thinking about the brand and the category and caring about the quality of a single frame. You'll enjoy setting strategy in one meeting and art-directing in the next. You get as much energy from building the system behind great work as from making it, and you can hold a room of executives as comfortably as a room of creatives. If you want real influence over business outcomes and a brand you can call your own, you'll feel at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lyrebird Health is transforming the quality and accessibility of healthcare by automating clinicians' most time-consuming tasks. We're building the medical intelligence layer for modern healthcare: a clinical AI platform that combines ambient real-time documentation, intelligent document management, clinical workflow automation, native patient data integrations across siloed health systems, and a communications layer that keeps clinicians and patients connected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thousands of clinicians across multiple disciplines use Lyrebird every day in environments where accuracy, safety, and time matter deeply. We give clinicians richer patient information at the right moment and lighten their mental load during consults, so they can focus on delivering better care. Everything we build is grounded in earning trust, reducing cognitive load, and delivering meaningful impact at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-own Lyrebird's brand strategy and lead its UK rollout. This covers positioning, media, communications and campaigns that grow brand preference and trust among UK clinicians and healthcare professionals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set and hold the creative quality and taste bar for everything Lyrebird makes globally, whether it's made in-house or by agencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the creative engine: the operations, workflows, playbooks and systems that let in-house and external teams produce world-class work at volume and pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Select, brief and manage creative and media agencies to a high standard, and decide what we build in-house and what we outsource.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and own a brand measurement framework for a clinical audience, and report on brand health against clear goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the research and partnerships agenda that helps build the medical AI category the right way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with growth, retention, product marketing, our clinical team, product and engineering, analytics, sales, customer success and our founders, so the brand holds together across every touchpoint.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior experience leading brand strategy and creative output, either at an agency or in-house at a growth-stage company, and a body of work you're proud of.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A high creative bar. You set the standard, art-direct, and give sharp direction that lifts the quality of a team's work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational brand media depth: planning, buying and optimising integrated campaigns across digital, OOH, streaming audio, social, professional media partnerships, conference sponsorships and sponsored content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creative operations and agency leadership. You've built the systems and managed the partners that let great work ship at pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An audience-first instinct backed by analytical rigour. You turn insight about a professional audience into positioning, media and creative that resonate, and you're comfortable with brand measurement, including brand lift and incrementality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong leadership and communication, and an AI-native approach. You build and develop talent, and you use AI across creative development, planning, research and reporting.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with healthcare or medical audience channels, such as medical associations, clinical publications and conference media.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in the UK or NHS healthcare market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with dashboards and marketing measurement tools such as Tableau, Sigma or Looker, and with marketing mix modelling or incrementality studies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The work you do here will shape how clinicians first come to know and trust Lyrebird, and that trust is what lets them bring it into the care they give. The stronger the brand and the work, the more clinicians reach for Lyrebird, and the more patients feel the difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building a team that reflects the diversity of the people who benefit from our work. We want Lyrebird to be a place where everyone feels safe, supported, and able to thrive. If you're from an underrepresented background in tech, we strongly encourage you to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lyrebird-health/head-of-brand-and-creative-united-kingdom-403240","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1792561215},{"slug":"research-scientist-protein-design-engineering-cambridge-ma-102745","company_name":"Dayhoff Labs","title":"Research Scientist, Protein Design & Engineering","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're reverse-engineering the origin of life — one of the great unsolved problems in science, and one we think AI finally makes tractable. Understanding this transition, from geochemistry to biochemistry, is what will let us orchestrate molecular networks and build systems that are more capable, adaptive, and efficient.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If we succeed, the applications are vast: catalysis, green synthesis, ab initio synthetic biology, programmable matter. Understanding and harnessing these processes could let ten billion of us thrive on this planet — and let life keep evolving beyond it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a small, diverse team of AI engineers, computational scientists, and bench scientists. We hold ourselves to the rigor of a research institute, but we ship like an engineering firm. Global team, HQs in Cambridge, MA and London, UK.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll engineer proteins to carry out useful chemistry, combining enzyme discovery, directed evolution, and experimental characterisation. You'll own the experimental cycle: choosing starting points, building variant libraries, developing screens, and establishing which changes improve function and why.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role working closely with our computational and ML teams. You'll test designed proteins at the bench, use experimental results to guide subsequent rounds, and develop enzymes with the activity, selectivity, and stability needed for their intended application. There’s no fixed screening pipeline to inherit — you'll help decide how we build it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and run protein engineering campaigns, from initial enzyme selection and library design through screening and characterisation of improved variants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and express variant libraries using site-directed, random, and combinatorial mutagenesis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop assays and high-throughput screens that reliably measure the properties we're trying to improve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Express, purify, and characterise proteins, measuring kinetics, substrate scope, selectivity, and stability under relevant reaction conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with computational scientists to test proposed designs, interpret successes and failures, and use the results to guide the next round.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop enzymatic reactions and cascades, identifying how enzyme performance, cofactors, and reaction conditions affect overall productivity.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're interested in the engineering campaigns you've run, the assays you've built, and what you learned from them. We care about:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of improving protein or enzyme function through directed evolution or rational engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical fluency in molecular biology, including cloning, library construction, mutagenesis, and recombinant protein expression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing and troubleshooting enzyme assays and screening workflows, with appropriate controls and follow-up validation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid grasp of enzyme mechanism, kinetics, and structure–function relationships, and the ability to use these to guide experiments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience independently taking projects through multiple design–build–test cycles and explaining what drove the results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Highly preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with industrial biocatalysis or engineering enzymes for demanding reaction conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating liquid handling and laboratory automation with high-throughput screening.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with biosensor-based screens, growth-based selection, or FACS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience testing computationally designed proteins and feeding experimental results back into design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with enzyme cascades, fermentation, or transferring enzymatic processes from the bench to larger scales.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Logistics</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time, on-site role in Cambridge, MA. Compensation is highly competitive. We're also able to sponsor visas for the right candidate.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/dayhoff-labs/research-scientist-protein-design-engineering-cambridge-ma-102745","tags":["Experimental"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Cambridge, MA","created_at":1792561214},{"slug":"senior-outsourced-sales-manager-vinted-go-acquisition-428716","company_name":"Vinteden","title":"Senior Outsourced Sales Manager: Vinted Go Acquisition","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vinted Go grows by signing new pick-up/drop-off locations, and a large share of that growth is delivered by external sales agencies. You will own that network: the agencies running our field sales, virtual calling and digital outreach across Europe and the US.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today these relationships are managed in a fragmented way. Your job is to turn them into one well-governed, high-performing extension of the acquisition team, with clear targets, a consistent operating rhythm and a single point of accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership role. You will act as an agency manager, performance analyst and budget owner, and above all as the guardian of the Vinted Go sales approach in every conversation an agency has on our behalf. You will build on the structure that already exists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency &amp;amp; Channel Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full relationship with every outsourced sales partner across countries: onboarding, day-to-day management, escalations and offboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the single point of accountability for agency sales results, replacing today&#39;s fragmented oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage contracts, SLAs and commercial terms, including pay-for-performance structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, select and onboard new sales agencies as we enter new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build one operating framework (reporting cadence, WBRs, MBRs, escalation paths) that works the same way across agencies, channels and countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track sales KPIs and SLAs per agency, channel and market: conversion, signed locations per rep, productivity, lead quality and adherence to the Vinted Go pitch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards that give real-time visibility into performance across the whole network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot underperforming agencies or markets early and drive corrective action plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate acquisition targets set by leadership into agency-level performance expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run calibration and quality assurance (call reviews, field ride-alongs) so every agency sells consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the outsourced sales budget across all agencies and countries: forecasting, spend tracking and variance reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze cost per outcome (CAC, cost per signed location, cost per hour) across agencies, channels and markets to drive efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find and execute cost optimizations without compromising quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on budget and performance regularly to finance and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale &amp;amp; Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the processes and governance needed to run a multi-agency, multi-country, multi-language sales network sustainably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain playbooks for opening new markets and onboarding new agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the acquisition team to align on targets, budgets and reporting standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior experience managing external sales agencies or outsourced sales teams (field sales, telesales, digital lead generation), ideally across several countries and vendors at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in sales, acquisition or growth in a high-velocity environment, so you know what good looks like on the ground&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of agency performance management: setting KPIs and SLAs, running WBRs and MBRs, and driving accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budget ownership: forecasting, tracking and optimizing spend across multiple vendors or cost centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort building structure and process from a relatively unstructured starting point&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, working easily in dashboards, reporting tools and a CRM to track performance and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and negotiation skills: you hold agencies accountable while keeping the partnership productive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across time zones and cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English; French and/or Spanish is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Outsourced sales is one of the main ways Vinted Go signs new locations at scale, and it is growing in every market we enter. This role brings order, accountability and cost discipline to that network, and lays the foundation for further international and product growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 working days of holiday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-contribution meal vouchers for each workday through a convenient meal card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Medical Coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/vinteden/senior-outsourced-sales-manager-vinted-go-acquisition-428716","tags":["Business & Commercial"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792594515},{"slug":"accounts-payable-specialist-paris-300749","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Accounts Payable Specialist","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Accounts Payable Specialist, you own the supplier-to-payment cycle for Harmattan AI's entities. You will build and improve AP processes rather than just run them. Working closely with Finance, Procurement and cost center managers, you keep supplier payments reliable and controls strong as the company's volumes and entities grow.</p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full supplier-to-payment cycle, from invoice receipt and coding to approval and payment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform three-way matching and resolve mismatches with Procurement and Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and validate payment runs (SEPA and international) in line with due dates and cash planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reconcile supplier accounts and investigate discrepancies or unallocated payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Answer supplier queries on payment status and disputes, verifying bank detail changes before any update.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve invoice capture, approval workflows and reporting, and drive AP automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen internal controls and fraud prevention across the AP process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep AP records and procedures documented to support audits and French accounting compliance.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2 to 4 years of experience in accounts payable, ideally in an industrial or high-growth environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid command of the full AP cycle, including invoice processing, matching, payment runs and supplier reconciliations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good knowledge of French accounting rules and VAT, including intra-EU and import transactions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with an ERP or accounting system; advanced Excel and familiarity with AP automation tools are a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multi-entity and multi-currency accounting is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigor and accuracy, with a strong sense of internal control and organization under tight deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomy and a process mindset: you spot inefficiencies, document procedures and propose improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative, service-oriented approach with buyers, cost center managers and suppliers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent French and professional English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/accounts-payable-specialist-paris-300749","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792593618},{"slug":"supply-planner-orly-453327","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Supply Planner","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Supply Planner, your role is crucial in optimising the flow of materials from suppliers into our operations. You function as the primary analytical link between strategic purchasing decisions and operational inventory needs. Your main mission is to ensure optimal stock availability (raw materials, components) while driving cost efficiency and minimising risks of shortages or obsolescence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You actively collaborate with the Procurement team to integrate market insights into tangible planning actions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><h3><strong>Operational Planning and Procurement Strategy Support</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demand Translation: Analyze sales forecasts and production schedules to accurately determine raw material and component requirements (MRP/DRP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supplier Ordering: Generate, send, and monitor purchase orders (POs) based on planning requirements, ensuring alignment with procurement contracts and volume agreements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inventory Optimization: Define, monitor, and adjust planning parameters (safety stock, reorder points, EOQ) in the ERP to maintain target inventory levels and reduce working capital.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Supplier Performance and Risk Management</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">OTD Monitoring: Track and report on supplier performance metrics (On Time Delivery - OTD, lead time compliance) and proactively highlight potential delivery risks to the Procurement Manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Risk Analysis: Identify and anticipate potential supply disruptions (e.g., transport delays, capacity issues) and develop mitigation plans in collaboration with the Purchasing team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dispute Coordination: Serve as the planning focal point for resolving delivery and quantity discrepancies with suppliers, escalating critical issues to the Procurement Manager.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Process Improvement and Reporting</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5e