afely and repeatedly source and produce energetics as we scale. You will work daily with systems, warhead and fuze engineers, as well as test facilities and partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the internal reference on energetic materials chemistry, properties and compatibility to guide material selection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Baseline the energetic materials requirements and material inventory across our products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate chemical stability, ageing and environmental sensitivity to define safe-for-use, storage and operational requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and oversee material qualification in line with NATO standards, internally and with external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run hands-on material characterization and build the laboratory capability, in-house or through partners, to support it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess supplier specifications, process capability and quality requirements to ensure repeatability and traceability, and manage inspections and non-conformances.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support warhead and fuze engineers in sourcing and preparing materials for prototype testing, and report results to systems engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build qualification frameworks and guidance for the wider team, and contribute to growing an internal materials team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s degree or PhD in Chemistry, Materials Science, Chemical Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of explosive materials, propellants and pyrotechnics, including explosive safety and hazardous materials handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with analytical techniques such as DSC, TGA, FTIR and Raman spectroscopy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience characterizing and evaluating materials in accordance with NATO qualification standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running qualification programs for materials used in pyrotechnic or energetic systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of materials manufacturing processes and quality controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/energetic-materials-scientist-munitions-lausanne-465601","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792593618},{"slug":"h3c-expert-fur-infrastruktur-migration-basel-429539","company_name":"Coopers Group AG","title":"H3C Expert für Infrastruktur Migration","description":"<p>................</p>Für ein anspruchsvolles Infrastruktur-Transformationsprojekt in Basel suchen wir eine:n erfahrene: <strong>H3C Expert</strong>. Im Rahmen des Projekts wird eine bestehende Server-, Storage- und Virtualisierungslandschaft durch moderne H3C-Lösungen ersetzt. Du übernimmst eine zentrale Rolle bei der Planung, Architektur und Umsetzung der neuen Infrastruktur und begleiten die Migration bestehender Systeme in die neue Zielumgebung.<p><strong>Deine Aufgaben:</strong></p><ul><li>Konzeption und Design der zukünftigen H3C-Infrastruktur</li><li>Planung und Durchführung von Migrationsprojekten im Bereich Compute, Storage und Virtualisierung</li><li>Implementierung und Konfiguration von H3C