<p>Our technology enables effective and reliable operation, monitoring, and analysis of high-temperature plasmas in fusion devices — which will one day provide clean, practically limitless power to the grid. We have spun out of EPFL’s Swiss Plasma Center and have just completed our pre-seed fundraise.</p>
<p>We are looking for a <strong>Senior Control Systems Engineer</strong> to join our founding team in Lausanne and help build our core technology.</p>
<p>This job is for you if you are a passionate engineer with deep knowledge cutting across real-time / embedded systems, software and hardware, and excited about building the systems to monitor and control real-world fusion plasmas.</p>
<h2>Tasks</h2>
<ul>
<li>Implement real-time control, analysis, data acquisition systems in the kHz to MHz range, as individual contributor and in a team.</li>
<li>Integrate solutions across a variety of company products and services as well as on our in-house test beds.</li>
<li>Provide technical leadership within a growing real-time control and software engineering team that you will help to build.</li>
<li>Translate customer needs into requirements and specifications.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Experience taking hard-real-time acquisition and control loops from incomplete requirements through to commissioning on hardware, in domains such as automotive, robotics, embedded, electrical and/or scientific instrumentation.</li>
<li>‘Full stack’: familiarity with all aspects of real-time technologies, from physical/DAQ, real-time software frameworks and middleware, real-time OS and integration.</li>
<li>Fluency in a mix of high-level and low-level languages such as C, C++, Rust, MATLAB/Simulink, Python. Obsession with code quality, testing and reliability.</li>
<li>Experience with distributed real-time systems, real-time networking and field buses and/or SCADA is an advantage.</li>
<li>Experience with embedded/μC/FPGA technologies and/or safety critical systems is an advantage.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Benefits</h2>
<ul>
<li>The unique opportunity to play a foundational role at a dynamic, fast-growing startup, shaping the technical solutions and products from the ground up.</li>
