nsiveness)&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Optimize&nbsp;carrier&nbsp;selection&nbsp;to improve margins&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Deliver insights &amp; improve decisions&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Ensure carrier data is&nbsp;accurate, complete, and usable&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Provide insights to support pricing, planning, and strategy&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Identify&nbsp;structural gaps and improvement opportunities in the network&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>Who You Are&nbsp;</strong></p><p>You’re&nbsp;commercially aware, proactive, and comfortable working at the intersection of operations and Sales.&nbsp;</p><p>You will thrive in this role if you:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Have 5–8 years of experience in transport, freight&nbsp;forwarding, or&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;coordination.&nbsp;</li><li>Have experience with carrier onboarding, communication, and daily operations.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Take a proactive approach to expanding carrier capacity on existing and new lanes.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Are comfortable working with KPIs and continuously improving performance (service, responsiveness, reliability).&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Have a system-first mindset and ensure tools are used effectively.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Understand how your work impacts Sales win-rate, margins, and competitiveness.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Are structured, responsive, and take ownership.&nbsp;</li><li>Professional level of English and Dutch.</li><li>Third European language is preferred (ideally German, French, Polish).&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Why join&nbsp;CtrlChain?&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Direct impact on win-rate, margins, and growth&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>High ownership and autonomy&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Work closely with Sales and commercial teams&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Fast-paced scale-up environment&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><strong>What We Offer&nbsp;</strong></p><p>✔ Competitive salary &amp; benefits<br> ✔ 26 vacation days<br> ✔ Fully paid pension plan &amp; tr