at you'll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Transport end to end: Running the full release train for your value stream: discovery, scoping, design, development, launch and post-launch tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run customer discovery yourself, in the field: Talk to rental companies about how they plan, staff and execute transport today: warehouse-to-venue routing, multi-stop and multi-vehicle loads, load order, crew and vehicle capacity, and the constraints that make equipment transport harder than generic delivery routing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the first sellable increment. Find the smallest thing customers will genuinely pay for, ship it, and be able to explain why that slice was the right first bet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and own a sequenced, evidence-based roadmap with the Head of Product, aligned to company goals and product strategy. And explain the prioritisation to sales, support and management so they can plan against it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate routing and logistics complexity into buildable scope: multi-stop optimisation, time windows, vehicle and crew capacity, mapping and routing APIs, and the build-vs-buy decisions that come with them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define success before you build it: Every feature carries a business goal, product briefs stay current, a live dashboard goes up at launch, and you drive go-to-market together with Product Marketing, Support, Sales and Content &amp; Community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/3c95dc18-9519-4446-b1af-13a805537681/Screenshot_2026-07-23_at_10.38.46.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we are looking for </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years as a Product Manager in B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've owned a product area end to end. From discovery through launch and post-launch tracking, not a backlog-only PO role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with operationally complex problems: routing, scheduling, fleet or capacity planning, supply chain, field service. A logistics background is a plus, not a must.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work from data. You can show how you set a success metric, what you did when it was missed, and how you make the business case behind a product call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run customer discovery yourself, not through a research team, and you can make and defend scope calls on partial evidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product experience in route optimisation, fleet management, field service or supply chain / TMS, or hands-on experience with mapping and routing APIs and platforms (Google Maps Platform, HERE, Mapbox, route-optimisation engines).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building a product domain or team from scratch (0-to-1), not only taking one over.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in the live event, AV or equipment rental industry, and/or Dutch, German or French.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What you’ll get </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on experience, plus 8% holiday allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A results-based bonus based on company performance (up to a full 13th month's salary)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 vacation days to recharge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earn an extra day of PTO for each year at Rentman, from your second anniversary up to five years.</p>