&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1800&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/databricks/enterprise-hunter-account-executive-benelux-amsterdam-76929","tags":["Enterprise Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792508123},{"slug":"system-architect-eindhoven-481897","company_name":"Deerns Groep BV","title":"System Architect","description":"<p><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em">Are you an experienced System Architect with a passion for intelligent building management systems, industrial automation, and safety-critical applications? At Deerns, you will have the opportunity to work on innovative and challenging projects that contribute to a smarter, safer, and more sustainable future. Read on and discover how you can make an impact.</span></strong><br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>The challenge</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">The System Architect for Intelligent Building Management Solutions and Industrial Automation plays a crucial role in designing integrated automation solutions for both buildings and industrial processes. This position involves developing safe, efficient, and future-ready systems that connect various installations, such as HVAC, lighting, access control, gas safety, and industrial process control. You will work closely with project teams, suppliers, and end-users to create innovative and sustainable solutions that meet the highest safety standards. </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Your responsibilities include:&nbsp;</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Developing automation architectures: Design scalable solutions for intelligent building management and process automation, including gas detection systems, safety mechanisms, and process control. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">System integration: Connect installations using protocols like BACnet, Modbus, KNX, and industrial standards such as OPC UA and PROFIBUS. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Gas safety and process safety: Develop solutions for gas detection, emergency shutdowns, ventilation integration, and fail-safe control systems for industrial environments. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Specification and standards management: Implement relevant standards for intelligent building management solutions, process automation, and safety systems, such as IEC 61511 (functional safety) and ATEX regulations. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Process optimization: Analyze and optimize industrial processes and systems to enhance efficiency, safety, and sustainability. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Stakeholder management: Collaborate effectively with various stakeholders, including clients, end-users, engineers, and project managers, ensuring solutions meet both functional and technical requirements. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Continuous learning and development: Stay updated on the latest innovations in smart technologies and automation, applying these to develop improved, future-proof solutions. • Technological consulting: Identify innovations to enhance performance and reliability in intelligent buildings and industrial environments. </p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Documentation and communication: Prepare technical documentation and communicate effectively with multidisciplinary teams and stakeholders. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>Required Skills and Competencies:</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Extensive knowledge of intelligent building management solutions, gas safety systems, and industrial process control.</p></li><li><p>Expertise in communication standards and protocols such as KNX, BACnet, Modbus, OPC UA, and PROFIBUS. </p></li><li><p>Proficiency in designing fail-safe systems and safety-critical applications. </p></li><li><p>Experience with IT networks and cybersecurity in automation environments. </p></li><li><p>Strong analytical skills and problem-solving abilities. </p></li><li><p>Flexibility and the ability to continuously adapt to technological advancements. </p></li><li><p>Excellent communication skills to clearly present complex technical issues</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>Education and Experience: </strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p>Bachelor’s or master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Automation Technology, or a related field. </p></li><li><p>Relevant experience in intelligent building management solutions, industrial automation, and safety-critical systems. This role combines technological innovation with safety-critical applications. As a System Architect, you will develop integrated solutions that maximize comfort, safety, efficiency, and sustainability in both buildings and industrial processes.<br></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>We offer</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">A position of 32-40 hours per week with a salary to match.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Challenging projects for leading clients in the Netherlands and internationally.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">A work environment in which innovation and sustainability are put into practice daily.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Attention to your own development and vitality with ample training and development opportunities, bicycle and sports arrangements, flexible working hours, 33 vacation days and the possibility of purchasing additional days.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Hybrid working, where you have the opportunity to alternate between working from home and the office.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">A team where cooperation and collegiality are priority, and where we interact informally.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW53972283 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">Sustainability is in our genes. This is expressed, for example, in a mobility policy where health and sustainability are most important. Many of our offices are located near public transport hubs, cycling is encouraged, and your travel expenses are reimbursed 100% on the basis of public transport.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>About Deerns</strong>&nbsp;<br>As an independent engineering firm, Deerns specializes in consultancy, design and implementation supervision in the fields of installation engineering, building physics, energy supply and sustainability. Our areas of expertise contribute to sustainable, intelligent and future-proof buildings that optimally support our clients' processes. We are responsible for designing the installations and realizing good comfort and a pleasant climate in a wide variety of buildings; from offices, to airports and from hospitals to data centers.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>In addition, Deerns has been named a World Class Workplace for 2026!</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0">&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW53972283 BCX0"><strong>Want to know more?</strong>&nbsp;<br>Would you like to know more about working at Deerns? Then contact Maarten Borgmeijer (Corporate Recruiter) at +31 6 11 66 75 44. Would you like to know more about the role itself? Then please contact Ester Vlielander (Unit Director Electronics / Data Centers / Life Sciences) at +31 6 50 73 68 41</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/deerns-groep-bv/system-architect-eindhoven-481897","tags":["Electronics"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Eindhoven, Noord-Brabant, Netherlands","created_at":1792506670},{"slug":"remote-hoofdmonteur-warmtepompen-85022","company_name":"DeWarmte","title":"Hoofdmonteur Warmtepompen","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij DeWarmte maken we slimme en betaalbare warmtepompen waarmee we woningen van het gas af helpen. We ontwerpen onze producten zelf, assembleren ze in Utrecht en zorgen samen met onze installatiepartners dat ze bij steeds meer mensen thuis komen te staan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We groeien hard. Tot nu toe worden al onze warmtepompen geïnstalleerd door externe partners, maar daar komt verandering in. We gaan onze eigen installatieteams opbouwen en zoeken daarom een <strong>Hoofdmonteur Warmtepompen</strong> die hierin het voortouw neemt.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent een ervaren monteur die graag zelf de handen uit de mouwen steekt, maar ook energie krijgt van het begeleiden van anderen. Je gaat samen met je team op pad, bent verantwoordelijk voor de kwaliteit van de installaties en helpt ons om steeds meer monteurs op te leiden.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je komt dus niet in een bestaand team terecht. Je helpt het team zelf opbouwen.</strong></p><h2><strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als Hoofdmonteur ben je verantwoordelijk voor de installatie van onze warmtepompen bij klanten thuis. Je begint met het leiden van ons eerste interne installatieteam en helpt ons om de komende jaren onze eigen installatiecapaciteit verder uit te bouwen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je installeert warmtepompen en leidt je team</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je gaat samen met een collega-monteur op pad om onze warmtepompen bij klanten thuis te installeren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent verantwoordelijk voor de volledige installatie, van de technische uitvoering en het oplossen van onverwachte problemen tot de oplevering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je zorgt dat installaties veilig, efficiënt en volgens onze kwaliteitsstandaarden worden uitgevoerd.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent het aanspreekpunt voor de klant tijdens de installatie. Je legt uit wat jullie doen, beantwoordt vragen en zorgt dat de klant met een goed gevoel achterblijft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je stemt waar nodig af met onze werkvoorbereiders en collega's op kantoor over planning, materialen en technische uitdagingen.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je bouwt mee aan ons interne installatieteam</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je begeleidt en traint nieuwe monteurs en helpt hen om zelfstandig installaties uit te kunnen voeren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je denkt mee over het aannemen van nieuwe collega's en hoe we ons installatieteam verder kunnen uitbreiden.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je helpt onze installatiestandaarden en werkwijzen verder te ontwikkelen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je signaleert wat er in de praktijk beter of slimmer kan en neemt initiatief om dit te verbeteren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je deelt feedback vanuit het veld met onze engineers, werkvoorbereiders en productontwikkelaars, zodat we onze producten en installaties continu kunnen verbeteren.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Wie zoeken wij?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We zoeken iemand die zijn vak goed verstaat, verantwoordelijkheid neemt en het leuk vindt om anderen beter te maken. Je hoeft niet eerder een heel team te hebben opgebouwd, maar je moet wel zin hebben om die uitdaging aan te gaan.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt ruime ervaring met het installeren van warmtepompen, cv-installaties of andere verwarmingssystemen. Ervaring met warmtepompen heeft een sterke voorkeur.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt een goede technische basis in installatietechniek, elektrotechniek en/of werktuigbouwkunde.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je kunt zelfstandig installaties uitvoeren, technische tekeningen lezen en onverwachte problemen oplossen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt ervaring met het begeleiden van andere monteurs, of bent klaar om die verantwoordelijkheid op je te nemen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je werkt nauwkeurig en veilig en vindt het belangrijk om goed werk af te leveren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je communiceert makkelijk met klanten en collega's en kunt technische zaken begrijpelijk uitleggen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je neemt initiatief, denkt in oplossingen en voelt je verantwoordelijk voor het eindresultaat.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je spreekt goed Nederlands en hebt rijbewijs B.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een relevante mbo-opleiding en certificeringen zoals VCA, NEN 3140 of CO-vakmanschap zijn mooi meegenomen. Heb je nog niet alle benodigde certificaten? Dan kijken we samen wat je nog kunt behalen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Wat bieden wij jou?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Een salaris van €4.000 tot €6.000 bruto per maand</strong> op basis van 40 uur, afhankelijk van je ervaring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Een sleutelrol in ons bedrijf:</strong> je wordt de eerste Hoofdmonteur van ons interne installatieteam en helpt dit verder uit te bouwen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Veel vrijheid en verantwoordelijkheid:</strong> je krijgt de ruimte om mee te denken over hoe we installeren, samenwerken en nieuwe monteurs opleiden.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Goed materiaal:</strong> een volledig uitgeruste werkbus en professioneel gereedschap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>26 vakantiedagen en 13 ADV-dagen</strong> op basis van 40 uur, met de mogelijkheid om te kiezen voor een hogere beloning in plaats van ADV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een goede pensioenregeling volgens de cao Metaal &amp; Techniek.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mogelijkheden om jezelf verder te ontwikkelen, zowel technisch als in het begeleiden en aansturen van een team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een betrokken team met korte lijnen, weinig bureaucratie en regelmatig leuke activiteiten, van borrels en teamuitjes tot onze jaarlijkse wintersport.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Waarom DeWarmte?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij DeWarmte geloven we dat verduurzaming pas echt werkt als het voor iedereen bereikbaar en aantrekkelijk is. Daarom ontwikkelen we slimme, betaalbare warmtepompen die we zelf ontwerpen en assembleren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We zijn een groeiend bedrijf waar veel gebeurt en waar je echt invloed hebt op hoe we dingen aanpakken. We houden van mensen die initiatief nemen, samenwerken en niet wachten tot iemand anders een probleem oplost.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als Hoofdmonteur krijg je de kans om vanaf het begin mee te bouwen aan onze eigen installatieorganisatie. Je werkt zelf aan mooie technische installaties, leidt nieuwe monteurs op en helpt bepalen hoe we dit in de toekomst op grotere schaal gaan doen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Klaar om samen met ons iets op te bouwen?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solliciteer en kom kennismaken. We vertellen je graag meer over DeWarmte, onze warmtepompen en onze plannen voor het interne installatieteam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €4K – €6K per month</p><ul><li> • €4K – €6K per month</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dewarmte/remote-hoofdmonteur-warmtepompen-85022","tags":["Installations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1792485618},{"slug":"plc-software-engineer-the-netherlands-enschede-370473","company_name":"HoSt Group Bioenergy Systems","title":"PLC Software Engineer - The Netherlands","description":"<figure><img style="width:263px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/c5kbn95coa/Logo_Bright_-_Full_colour.png"></figure><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>Ready to build the software behind real-world renewable energy installations?</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">At Bright Renewables, your PLC software doesn’t stay behind a desk. You’ll see it come to life in complex industrial installations for renewable gas and CO₂ technologies.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">As a <strong>PLC</strong> <strong>Software Engineer</strong>, <span style="color:#5a5f72">you’ll be involved in the complete automation lifecycle - from software design and programming to testing, commissioning, troubleshooting, and optimization.</span></p><p>You’ll have the opportunity to contribute to technical decisions, help shape our automation standards, and work alongside experienced colleagues as part of an international software engineering team of around 10 engineers. Together, you’ll collaborate across the Netherlands, Latvia, and Poland to develop and deliver reliable, innovative automation solutions.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><strong><br>Why this role? </strong></h3><p class="isSelectedEnd">You’ll get the opportunity to:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Own your solutions</strong> - <span style="color:#5a5f72">contribute to software solutions throughout the project lifecycle, from design and programming to testing and commissioning;</span></p></li><li><p><strong>Work on real installations</strong> - solve automation challenges in complex renewable energy plants;</p></li><li><p><strong>Have technical influence</strong> - <span style="color:#5a5f72">contribute to software standards, templates, concepts, and ways of working, within a team that values collaboration and embraces innovative ideas from everyone;</span></p></li><li><p><strong>Keep developing</strong> - work alongside experienced Electrical and Software Engineers and continue building your technical expertise;</p></li><li><p><strong>Work internationally</strong> - collaborate with colleagues and project teams in the Netherlands, Poland, Latvia and beyond, including regular international travel to visit our offices and project sites;</p></li><li><p><strong>Choose what works for you</strong> - work 32 or 40 hours per week, with flexible starting times and opportunities to work from home;</p></li><li><p><strong>Make an impact</strong> - use your automation expertise in technologies that contribute directly to the energy transition.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;">What will you do?</h3><p class="isSelectedEnd">As a PLC Software Engineer, you design, develop, test, and commission <strong>PLC and SCADA control systems</strong> for technologies such as gas upgrading and CO₂ liquefaction.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You report directly to the Manager E&amp;I and Software and work closely with Electrical Engineers, Process Engineers and fellow Software Engineers</span><span style="color:#242424">.</span></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Depending on your experience, you’ll also have the opportunity to take more technical ownership, contribute to software concepts and standards, and support colleagues with complex automation challenges.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>Your responsibilities include:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Designing, programming, testing, and commissioning <strong>PLC and SCADA systems</strong>;</p></li><li><p>Developing control software for gas upgrading, CO₂ liquefaction, and other renewable energy technologies;</p></li><li><p>Taking ownership of your software from engineering through commissioning;</p></li><li><p>Testing and troubleshooting software during commissioning and operation;</p></li><li><p>Analyzing and resolving software and control-related issues in existing installations;</p></li><li><p>Implementing software updates and optimizations;</p></li><li><p>Supporting Service Engineers with more complex automation and software questions;</p></li><li><p>Contributing to software standards, templates, and automation concepts;</p></li><li><p>Working closely with Electrical Engineers, Software Engineers, and other technical disciplines;</p></li><li><p>Sharing knowledge and supporting colleagues within the engineering team.</p></li></ul><h3 style="text-align:start;"></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h3></h3><h3>What do you bring?</h3><p class="isSelectedEnd">We’re looking for someone who enjoys solving technical challenges and wants to take responsibility for their own engineering work.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Ideally, you have:</p><ul><li><p>A completed technical education in automation, mechatronics, electrical engineering, computer science, or a related field;</p></li><li><p>Several years of experience in PLC/SCADA engineering within an industrial environment;</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience in PLC programming, ideally with Siemens S7 and TIA Portal, combined with knowledge of WinCC SCADA, industrial communication networks, and remote access solutions.</p></li><li><p>Experience with commissioning and troubleshooting industrial installations;</p></li><li><p>A good understanding of automation architectures and industrial control systems;</p></li><li><p>Good command of English, both spoken and written;</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of OT security is a plus.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h3>What’s in it for you?</h3><p class="isSelectedEnd">We want to give you the technical freedom and working environment to do your best engineering work.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">You can expect:</p><ul><li><p>A competitive salary based on your experience and technical background;</p></li><li><p>The option to work 32 or 40 hours per week;</p></li><li><p>Flexible starting times between 7:00 and 9:00 a.m. ;</p></li><li><p>Ample opportunities to work from home, including a one-time €250 allowance to set up your home office;</p></li><li><p>An attractive annual profit-sharing scheme for employees with at least 12 months of service;</p></li><li><p>An excellent pension scheme;</p></li><li><p>8% annual holiday allowance;</p></li><li><p>A commuting allowance of €0.23 per kilometer, in accordance with our employment conditions;</p></li><li><p>A high level of autonomy and responsibility;</p></li><li><p>Plenty of opportunities for technical and professional development;</p></li><li><p>An international engineering environment with both experienced professionals and engineers earlier in their careers;</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to work with renewable energy technologies and contribute directly to the energy transition;</p></li><li><p>A bike lease program and rewards for cycling to work;</p></li><li><p>A modern, sustainably built working environment in Hengelo.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>About Bright Renewables</h3><p>Bright Renewables develops and delivers technologies for renewable gas and CO₂ capture, providing solutions from engineering and realization through to service and maintenance. Our installations convert biogas into renewable natural gas and capture, purify, and liquefy CO₂ for industrial reuse.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We are part of <strong>HoSt Group</strong>, a family-owned Dutch company operating internationally in renewable energy technology.</p><p>For you, that means working on international projects with the opportunities of a global organization, while keeping the short communication lines, technical freedom, and personal approach of a family-owned company.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Interested?</h3><p class="isSelectedEnd">We’d like to get to know you.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Apply by submitting your CV and motivation through the application button. Within 14 days, we’ll let you know whether we’d like to invite you for an interview.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Would you first like to know more about the technology, team, or day-to-day work?</p><p>Contact Wybren Broersma, Manager E&amp;I and Software, or Natalia Wisniewska, Corporate Recruiter, at +31 88 460 90 80.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Build software. See it running. Make an impact on renewable energy.</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/host-group-bioenergy-systems/plc-software-engineer-the-netherlands-enschede-370473","tags":["Bright Renewables"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Enschede, Overijssel, Netherlands","created_at":1792475488},{"slug":"ai-engineer-amsterdam-473945","company_name":"Gain","title":"AI Engineer","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who are we?</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Gain is the Private Markets Super App, a connected global platform transforming how leading investors, advisors, and corporates source, evaluate, and execute deals. By combining investment-grade intelligence, AI-powered workflows, and proprietary data in one unified platform, Gain enables top deal teams to move faster, reduce risk, and build conviction with confidence.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Gain is trusted across more than $1 trillion of private capital, used by 100% of MBB and Big Four firms, and by 80% of the world’s top 20 M&amp;A advisory houses.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Recognized for fast innovation and impact, Gain has been named both US and EU Data Provider of the Year by PE Wire, awarded Global Financial Market Review’s Best Use of AI in Finance, and ranked in Sifted’s Top 100 Fastest-Growing Companies, the Forbes 1000, and the Deloitte Technology Fast 50. Gain operates globally with offices in New York, London, Amsterdam, Frankfurt, Warsaw, and Bangalore.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">How we work</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Predicting what isn't published.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Many private companies publish little or no financial detail. Across a database of more than 5 million companies, we predict revenue and EBITDA from sparse labels, and we predict whether and when a company will be bought or sold, which is a time-to-event problem with censored data.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Agents on a messy web.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Our agents search, navigate and extract company data points from sources that contradict each other, then decide which source to trust before committing to an answer.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Quality that holds while everything underneath moves.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> We're provider-agnostic. Model choices follow the evals, and we switch LLMs when the numbers say so. That only works if the evals are trusted.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">What will you do?</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">The work is roughly half LLM agents and half custom ML, leaning slightly toward agents.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">The design of our agent pipelines: architecture, tools, and which model for which task. You'll shape the technical direction with our AI Lead.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">The evaluation behind agents and models: offline reference sets, live production evals, and the call on whether an improvement is real.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Our prediction models for financials and deals: features, validation, retraining, and knowing when a simpler model wins.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Getting work into production: trace where pipelines fail and fix the weakest links first, with compute, memory and model cost in view.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Raising the bar in the team through design reviews, pairing, and an eval-first habit that sticks.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">In your first six months you'll own the evals for our agent pipelines, propose where we invest next, and ship measurable improvements to both the agents and the prediction models.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who are you?</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You've built and owned ML systems in production for years, typically 6+ in ML or software engineering.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">In the last 1–2 years you've shipped LLM agents or pipelines that real users depend on, not demos.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have modelling judgement. You've dealt with leakage, distribution shift and calibration on real data.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You measure before you claim. You can build an evaluation set and tell an honest improvement from a lucky one.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You care about the user outcome more than the technique. Ideas without a clear customer benefit don't get built here, however interesting.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Nice to have: time-to-event modelling, noisy or conflicting data sources, financial or private-company data. No finance background needed.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">The team</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">You'll join our Data &amp; AI team of six and report to Renan, our AI Lead who's been building production models for &gt;10 years. Our engineering team runs the infrastructure, and you shape what runs on it.</span><br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">The stack</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Core:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Python (async, fully typed with Pydantic) and FastAPI</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">LLMs:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> multiple providers behind our own provider-agnostic layer, with Pydantic AI for typed agents. </span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Evals and observability:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Pydantic Evals and Logfire</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Data:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> PostgreSQL with pgvector</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Cloud:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> GCP (Cloud Run, Cloud Tasks), Docker, GitHub Actions</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What do we offer?</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">base salary</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> and </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">annual bonus</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> linked to your performance / OKRs</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Attractive benefits including health &amp; wellbeing allowance, work-from-home budget, learning &amp; coaching benefits, etc.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Flexible hybrid working model with 3 days per week in our Amsterdam office&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Healthy work-life balance allowing for planability and personal commitments&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Chance to grow with the company gaining increasing responsibilities, supported by lots of coaching and a feedback-driven approach&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Tremendous learning and career progression opportunities&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">International environment with hubs in New York, London, Amsterdam, Frankfurt, Warsaw, and Bangalore</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Culture of trust, ownership and standard of excellence and a fun working atmosphere with regular outings and events&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Post product-market fit and aspiring unicorn status - this is an excellent time to join &amp; grow with us!</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Does this sound like a perfect match?</span></st